{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron","id":773619,"title":"Better defined cold iron?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-24T21:02:57-08:00","id":773619,"title":"Better defined cold iron?","content":"Playing Changeling the Lost I have noticed that it never really accurately defined what Cold Iron was, it's been defined incredibly inconsistently.<br /> <br /> Traits:<ul><li>Cannot be &quot;machine cut&quot;</li> <li>Cannot be shaped by &quot;Magic&quot;</li> <li>Cannot not be &quot;Steel&quot;</li> <li>Cannot be an &quot;Alloy&quot;</li> <li>Must be &quot;Relatively&quot; or &quot;Largely&quot; Pure Iron</li> </ul><br /> Examples:<ul><li>Wrought Iron</li> <li>&quot;Meteoric Iron&quot; AKA Antitaenite, Kamacite, Taenite, and Tetrataenite alloys.</li> </ul><br /> Neither of the examples stated conform to the traits of what Cold Iron supposedly is, much less &quot;Hand-Wrought&quot; which I believe outlines quite poor conceptual work on the part of the developer. Furthermore in Rites of Spring the books essentially recognizes it's error and gives a cop-out say &quot;Well we didn't mean relatively pure iron! It's effectiveness depends on what you call it!&quot; This to me seems to smack of a lack of proper research over what exactly Iron and Steel are. It more or less forces you to ask your storyteller to fill in the obvious logical gaps that the book left in, which is just another &quot;rules thing&quot; that the storyteller has to worry about in running changeling. I'd like to see the definition of cold iron at least <b>be internally consistent with it's own examples</b> in the new edition.<br /> <br /> As to a comment on it's practicality, I kind of get why it's setting a (quite literal) impossible standard, because of the ubiquitous nature of Steels and other Iron Alloys in the modern world. But it comes across as a <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GLjcxVeNb3I&amp;feature=youtu.be&amp;t=8s\" target=\"_blank\"><b><i><u>quite blatant rule patch.</u></i></b></a>, and I do not believe that it is to the game's credit. It just comes off as... video-gamey? Almost like Steel's been nerfed in the patch-notes of reality for the new Arcadia update.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyone else have similar feelings about the vague nature of &quot;Cold Iron&quot; in the original rule set?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","user":"ReshyShira","date":". 11-25-2015, 12:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T22:34:10-08:00","id":773656,"title":"","content":"It was definitely pretty inconsistent in 1e. I'd be willing to bet that 2e will have it more clearly defined.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T22:36:19-08:00","id":773658,"title":"","content":"I suppose it would be nice to have a consistent definition, but it was never really something I worried about; we just picked a definition (hand-wrought, reasonably pure iron) and ran with it. Yeah, iron/steel is pretty common, but vampires are weak against wood and fire - hardly rare. Werewolves with silver, I suppose, but that didn't really add that much punch anyway - sure, they could heal lethal, but one/two a turn? Hunter cell with a couple guys with shotguns could probably take out a werewolf in a turn or two anyway, even with the healing. Plus changelings, while they can be epically powerful in combat, it never struck me as their 'thing', so then having an easily accessible weakess was never really a problem for me, conceptually. Besides, it's not like it's ever been defined consistently in myth (although just 'iron' seems to one of the more common ones).<br /> <br /> But yeah, consistent would be nice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T00:33:56-08:00","id":773705,"title":"","content":"The truth in the real world is that wrought iron isn't rare because it is actually rare, it's rare because steel is so superior that only niche markets deal in anything else. You can buy silver at any fancy store but asking for wrought iron is almost like asking for a paper fork, sure you could do it but why bother.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T01:39:59-08:00","id":773739,"title":"","content":"Besides, the impact of the bane on a Changeling is rather limited. A normal bullet or steel dagger hurts just as much. The only time it matters is when you try to imprison one since it impacts their Contracts. It certainly has never come up in my games as of yet, except the one time one of the characters was put in a cold iron cage and at that time nobody cared which of all of those it was.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I am all for a good definition since it would not be too hard. It is just that it is not particularly high on my wishlist <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T02:50:42-08:00","id":773769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madfox11</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=773739#post773739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides, the impact of the bane on a Changeling is rather limited. A normal bullet or steel dagger hurts just as much. The only time it matters is when you try to imprison one since it impacts their Contracts. It certainly has never come up in my games as of yet, except the one time one of the characters was put in a cold iron cage and at that time nobody cared which of all of those it was.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I am all for a good definition since it would not be too hard. It is just that it is not particularly high on my wishlist <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>And it also pierces magical protections, like that granted by Stone 5, Elemental 2, Vainglory 4 and every single Hedgespun armour. So yeah, better definition please, as the original one is horrible and shows zero understanding of metallurgy. Steel is just pure iron and &quot;cold iron&quot; is poetic term, it doesn't mean anything as you can't work any iron without heat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1274-crazy_ivan","name":"Crazy_Ivan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T03:02:12-08:00","id":773777,"title":"","content":"Steel is an alloy of iron and carbon. Not &quot;pure iron&quot; by any stretch of the imagination.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T08:05:25-08:00","id":773970,"title":"","content":"Unless I'm mis-remembering, Steel actual has more Iron content than Iron you find natural anyways. So unless they mean atomically pure (just the element 26, Iron), Steel should actually work <i>better</i>. And if they do mean pure 26, that's practically impossible, since it will bond to the oxygen in air fair quickly. <hr /><br /> Honestly, I've always cared more about the Iron content (&quot;Cold Iron&quot; being a poetic description, oft used for the sensation of having a room temperature section of conductive material inserted into one's body). Iron itself is a fun element (being the point at which fusion nor fission nets your more energy).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 11-25-2015, 11:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T08:17:18-08:00","id":773978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=773777#post773777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Steel is an alloy of iron and carbon. Not &quot;pure iron&quot; by any stretch of the imagination.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me break it down:<br /> <br /> Iron Ores (All of these deal Aggravated damage to Fae):<br /> Magnetite - 72.4% Iron Content<br /> Hematite - 69.9% Iron Content<br /> Goethite - 62.9% Iron Content<br /> Limonite <b>-</b> 59.8% Iron Content<br /> Siderite - 48.2% Iron Content<br /> <br /> &quot;Meteorite Iron&quot; (All of these are considered Cold Iron):<br /> Antitaenite - 60% to 80% Iron Content<br /> Kamacite - 90% to 95% Iron Content<br /> Taenite - 35% to 80% Iron Content<br /> Tetrataenite - [Unlisted]<br /> <br /> Smelted Iron (With exception of Wrought, doesn't work on Fae):<br /> Pig Iron - 95.5% to 96.5% Iron Content<br /> Cast Iron - 93.5% to 97% Iron Content<br /> Wrought Iron - 97.92% Iron Content<br /> <br /> Steels (Does not work on Fae):<br /> Wootz Steel - 98% to 99% Iron Content<br /> Low-Carbon Steel - 99.895% to 99.97% Iron Content<br /> Medium-Carbon Steel - 99.7% to 99.4% Iron Content<br /> High-Carbon Steel - 99.3% to 97.5% Iron Content<br /> Ultra-High-Carbon Steel - 97% Iron Content<br /> Stainless Steel - 50% to 89.5% Iron Content<br /> Eglin Steel - 84.463% to 90% Iron Content<br /> <br /> <br /> The list of steels go on and on and on. See how there is no rhyme or reason to the actual iron content? The only reason why I can think that it wouldn't work for steel is because the process of Smelting <b>removes the magnetic properties of the iron</b>. However, you can get those properties back by <b>hammering it</b><b>, </b>which might make sense why &quot;Hand-wrought&quot; weapons are extra effective, since they have a stronger magnetic pull. However, that means that you could take already tempered steel and restore it's magnetic properties again and restoring it's effectiveness against Fae?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","user":"ReshyShira","date":". 11-25-2015, 11:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T08:24:43-08:00","id":773983,"title":"","content":"There's no rhyme or reason to the True Fae, arguably that's the point. They're beings of stories and whimsy, not chemistry.<br /> <br /> As for defining the weapons necessary, you described it in your first post. Iron that has been forged by hand and tool, without the assistance of machines or magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-25-2015, 11:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T08:33:51-08:00","id":773990,"title":"","content":"This sounds like something the Null Mysteriis would love to research. Is it the Iron content? The magnetic properties? Something else? Let's find out!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T08:34:32-08:00","id":773991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=773983#post773983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no rhyme or reason to the True Fae, arguably that's the point. They're beings of stories and whimsy, not chemistry.<br /> <br /> As for defining the weapons necessary, you described it in your first post. Iron that has been forged by hand and tool, without the assistance of machines or magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're beings of stories from long ago when we knew little about the world. One of the reasons why Iron is supposed to be effective against them is because smelted, highly pure iron is unnatural and thus the antithesis of the Fae. Inverting that in Changeling the Lost seems to be missing the point of why they possess said vulnerability in the first place.<br /> <br /> Also my dear friend, everything is chemistry. Iron is a chemical element. Chromium is a chemical element, Oxygen is a chemical element. It goes on and on. I'm not necessarily asking for Onyx Path to hire a chemist to explain how it <b>might</b> work, but just to take maybe a day or two to research on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T08:37:04-08:00","id":773993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=773983#post773983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no rhyme or reason to the True Fae, arguably that's the point. They're beings of stories and whimsy, not chemistry.<br /> <br /> As for defining the weapons necessary, you described it in your first post. Iron that has been forged by hand and tool, without the assistance of machines or magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>But machines <i>are</i> tools. As, arguably, is magic. And hands are, again arguably, machines (albeit biological ones).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T08:37:21-08:00","id":773994,"title":"","content":"Magnetism. <br /> <br /> <i>Magnetism?</i><br /> <br /> Are you serious? <br /> <br /> Just... No.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T08:42:02-08:00","id":773999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=773994#post773994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Magnetism.<br /> <br /> <i>Magnetism?</i><br /> <br /> Are you serious?<br /> <br /> Just... No.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Well, it obviously disrupts whatever electo-magnetic field let's them repel standard ordinance. I'm writing it up in my thesis.&quot; -Doug Woolscott, Null Mysteriis researcher.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T08:43:04-08:00","id":774002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=773990#post773990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This sounds like something the Null Mysteriis would love to research. Is it the Iron content? The magnetic properties? Something else? Let's find out!</div> </div> </div> </div>I like to think of myself as Agatha.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://www.girlgeniusonline.com/ggmain/strips/ggmain20081205b.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=773994#post773994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Magnetism.<br /> <br /> <i>Magnetism?</i><br /> <br /> Are you serious?<br /> <br /> Just... No.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Why not? Magnets are often used to simulate magic tricks (think telekinesis, <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=A1vyB-O5i6E\" target=\"_blank\">levitation</a>, etc.) I don't see why it <b>couldn't</b> work against Fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T08:44:57-08:00","id":774005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=773705#post773705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The truth in the real world is that wrought iron isn't rare because it is actually rare, it's rare because steel is so superior that only niche markets deal in anything else. You can buy silver at any fancy store but asking for wrought iron is almost like asking for a paper fork, sure you could do it but why bother.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's true. But it's also true that you can improvise with any old fireplace poker or tongs. Those things are always iron (mass produced or not).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T08:50:04-08:00","id":774011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=773970#post773970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless I'm mis-remembering, Steel actual has more Iron content than Iron you find natural anyways. So unless they mean atomically pure (just the element 26, Iron), Steel should actually work <i>better</i>. And if they do mean pure 26, that's practically impossible, since it will bond to the oxygen in air fair quickly. <hr /><br /> Honestly, I've always cared more about the Iron content (&quot;Cold Iron&quot; being a poetic description, oft used for the sensation of having a room temperature section of conductive material inserted into one's body). Iron itself is a fun element (being the point at which fusion nor fission nets your more energy).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Cast iron is going to be mostly pure since many of the impurities are either burnt away or separated during smelting. The whole smelting process and relative softness of iron (which was really rather hard and holds a better edge when compared to bronze) was one of the driving forces behind the invention of steel. In some galactic twist of irony the semi-conducter revolution went through this same process where at first we though almost pure silicon was the way to go when making microchip and then realized we can get way better performance when we adulterate the silicon with other materials and eventually replaced most semi-conductor manufacturing with gallium-arsenide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T08:52:54-08:00","id":774013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774002#post774002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why not? Magnets are often used to simulate magic tricks (think telekinesis, <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=A1vyB-O5i6E\" target=\"_blank\">levitation</a>, etc.) I don't see why it <b>couldn't</b> work against Fae.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://i2.kym-cdn.com/entries/icons/original/000/013/034/yeahsciencebitch.PNG\" target=\"_blank\">Appropriate</a>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T08:53:45-08:00","id":774014,"title":"","content":"I have to agree, it is kind of frustrating. Another question that I have is whether or not you can use magic to &quot;just&quot; make a meteorite fall near you without taking away the Bane quality against the Gentry. You haven't started the forging yet, so as long as you only use your hands and tools, it should work, right?<br /> <br /> Also, how do you separate tool from machine in this forging? Is it a maximum number of moving parts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 11-25-2015, 11:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T08:55:36-08:00","id":774017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=773991#post773991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're beings of stories from long ago when we knew little about the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only if the Storyteller wants them to be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One of the reasons why Iron is supposed to be effective against them is because smelted, highly pure iron is unnatural and thus the antithesis of the Fae. </div> </div> </div>Or due to iron's curse, or the hope of man. The books are pretty clear that no one knows why iron affects them, just as they're unclear on what, exactly, the True Fae are.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also my dear friend, everything is chemistry. Iron is a chemical element. Chromium is a chemical element, Oxygen is a chemical element. It goes on and on. I'm not necessarily asking for Onyx Path to hire a chemist to explain how it <b>might</b> work, but just to take maybe a day or two to research on it. </div> </div> </div>And the research means nothing, because the chemical composition of it doesn't mean anything in terms of the True Fae. Steel has more iron in it than 'pure iron,' but steel is steel, and because of that, it's not iron, no matter how pure or cold forged it is.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But machines are tools. As, arguably, is magic. And hands are, again arguably, machines (albeit biological ones).</div> </div> </div> </div>Some machines apparently don't count and some do. Hands and hammer and fire are acceptable. Magic is not.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T08:56:08-08:00","id":774018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=773991#post773991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're beings of stories from long ago when we knew little about the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're beings of stories from yesterday, too, you know. Pulling the &quot;we know more about the world&quot; card doesn't work when the fae have continued to be coalesced forces of chaos and the byproducts of their interaction in an ever-shifting dreamscape of declarative reality and its immediate neighbors since time immemorial.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T08:56:21-08:00","id":774019,"title":"","content":"I have to say, as a storyteller I think the important factor is the &quot;hand wrought&quot; part and I would count any steel weapon as being a wrought iron weapon so long as it was hand-forged.<br /> <br /> Those are going to be relatively rare outside of Rennaissance Fairs. And even there, more of the steel thingies are mass-produced than people realize.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T09:04:33-08:00","id":774030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774017#post774017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Steel has more iron in it than 'pure iron,' but steel is steel, and because of that, it's not iron, no matter how pure or cold forged it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is, quite literally, semantics. Steel <i>is</i> Iron. As is wrought iron, pig iron, and many other things. I can call iron &quot;grey-metal&quot; - does it stop loosing its effect? Is this consensus driven? As what point does it have an effect?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T09:08:23-08:00","id":774032,"title":"","content":"If you ever discover something true about the True Fae, it retroactively stops being true out of spite.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774030#post774030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is, quite literally, semantics. Steel <i>is</i> Iron. As is wrought iron, pig iron, and many other things. I can call iron &quot;grey-metal&quot; - does it stop loosing its effect? Is this consensus driven? As what point does it have an effect?</div> </div> </div> </div>The point at which you started DEALING WITH THE FUCKING FAE.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T09:10:13-08:00","id":774035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774017#post774017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Only if the Storyteller wants them to be.<br /> <br /> Or due to iron's curse, or the hope of man. The books are pretty clear that no one knows why iron affects them, just as they're unclear on what, exactly, the True Fae are.<br /> <br /> And the research means nothing, because the chemical composition of it doesn't mean anything in terms of the True Fae. Steel has more iron in it than 'pure iron,' but steel is steel, and because of that, it's not iron, no matter how pure or cold forged it is.<br /> <br /> Some machines apparently don't count and some do. Hands and hammer and fire are acceptable. Magic is not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Obviously the True Fae are based off out folk lore, which usually has Iron as a way to ward them off. Somehow though, White Wolf decided to focus on the &quot;Cold&quot; rather than the &quot;Iron&quot; part. I'm fairly certain if you imprisoned a Fae and cut off it's hand it'd have a chemical composition, it might be a foreign element but it exists. Who knows, maybe the True Fae are some kind of Silicon Lifeform. Suffice to say though, they exist so they're made of something. Whatever that something is. If they were immaterial then they couldn't interact with the world. They can, so they're obviously material in some degree.<br /> <br /> On the &quot;Steel&quot; is &quot;Steel&quot; thing I don't see why it matters what it's called. It's still made of iron, and steel can be Cold-Worked. If your thought is &quot;Well names do matter&quot; then make some slightly different composition alloy that's primarily made of iron and call it iron, bam done.<br /> <br /> Fire is not acceptable, it even says so. If it's been &quot;heated&quot; it's not &quot;cold iron&quot; according to the book. But somehow, Meteorites are still &quot;Cold Iron&quot; for no explained reason.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774018#post774018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're beings of stories from yesterday, too, you know. Pulling the &quot;we know more about the world&quot; card doesn't work when the fae have continued to be coalesced forces of chaos and the byproducts of their interaction in an ever-shifting dreamscape of declarative reality and its immediate neighbors since time immemorial.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm talking about the story from where &quot;Cold Iron&quot; was actually mentioned, Iron in general has always been antithetical to supernatural things. According to folklore, anyway. <b>Why should steel lose this property?</b>The only reason I can think of is to balance out humanity, which is again a kind of obvious rule patch &quot;Well you already have so many iron products in the world, so we nerfed steel to make it fair to the poor Faeries who whined too much on the God-Machine's personal forum.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774032#post774032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you ever discover something true about the True Fae, it retroactively stops being true out of spite.<br /> <br /> <br /> The point at which you started DEALING WITH THE FUCKING FAE.</div> </div> </div> </div>Last I checked True Fae are still vulnerable to &quot;Cold Iron&quot; (whatever that means) and is a well known vulnerability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T09:12:51-08:00","id":774038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774035#post774035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Well you already have so many iron products in the world, so we nerfed steel to make it fair to the poor Faeries who whined too much on the God-Machine's personal forum.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That could easily be more or less exactly what happened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T09:17:18-08:00","id":774040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=773990#post773990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This sounds like something the Null Mysteriis would love to research. Is it the Iron content? The magnetic properties? Something else? Let's find out!</div> </div> </div> </div>I will note that I wanted to do a Changeling that might work with them (Probably from a distance, but still), but finding a Changeling game is difficult for me. It's not nearly as popular it seems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T09:39:40-08:00","id":774062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774035#post774035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obviously the True Fae are based off out folk lore, which usually has Iron as a way to ward them off. Somehow though, White Wolf decided to focus on the &quot;Cold&quot; rather than the &quot;Iron&quot; part. I'm fairly certain if you imprisoned a Fae and cut off it's hand it'd have a chemical composition, it might be a foreign element but it exists. Who knows, maybe the True Fae are some kind of Silicon Lifeform. Suffice to say though, they exist so they're made of something. Whatever that something is. If they were immaterial then they couldn't interact with the world. They can, so they're obviously material in some degree.</div> </div> </div> </div>Immaterial things interact with the world of darkness all the time. There's no guarantee a Fae's anything would have a chemical composition. Sure, in real life, you take a drop of water, divide it down and eventually get your molecule and can even divide that down to its component atoms. But a true fae could just be a drop of water, and you divide that down and just get smaller drops of water, without any sign of molecules or atoms. And yes, at that point you can say that it isn't water, or at least isn't h2o but you can drink it and it sustains you, you can freeze it and it turns to ice, you can boil it and it turns to steam, and you can give it back to the True Fae it came from but it doesn't matter because she grew more.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On the &quot;Steel&quot; is &quot;Steel&quot; thing I don't see why it matters what it's called. It's still made of iron, and steel can be Cold-Worked. If your thought is &quot;Well names do matter&quot; then make some slightly different composition alloy that's primarily made of iron and call it iron, bam done. </div> </div> </div>It's not just the name, it's the concept behind it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T09:43:45-08:00","id":774066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774062#post774062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not just the name, it's the concept behind it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes. Which the new &quot;totally-not-an-alloy&quot; maker is co-opting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T09:45:44-08:00","id":774069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774066#post774066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yes. Which the new &quot;totally-not-an-alloy&quot; maker is co-opting.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They're just co-opting the name, you're describing that in your quotes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T09:49:43-08:00","id":774072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774069#post774069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> They're just co-opting the name, you're describing that in your quotes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, no one is saying it <i>isn't</i> cold iron. And it is iron, people will call it iron, they aren't calling it anything else, theretofore True Fae will eat aggravated damage. (Insane Troll Logic cuts both ways)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T09:49:57-08:00","id":774073,"title":"","content":"This whole debate about what scientific property of iron is truly responsible for dealing aggravated damage to the Gentry strongly reminds me of another eldritch entity: <a href=\"http://www.scp-wiki.net/scp-2845\" target=\"_blank\"><b>SCP-2845 (AKA The Stag).</b></a> The ways that the Stag controls living and inert matter is pointed out in the article as impossible, according to our understanding of chemistry and biology. They had to consult a shaman of sorts to explain how the hell this Thing worked, and he essentially described how many supernatural phenomena in the NWOD function, including the Gentry to a fair extent:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Rituals do not work because of some underlying laws, such as those that science operates on. Rituals work because they are rituals. They work because an arbitrary set of criteria has been met with exacting care. Belief that meeting these arbitrary criteria achieves a certain end assigns power to the ritual. The actions that were once meaningless now have been assigned Meaning through their repetition and application.<br /> <br /> This is how one seals away a god, and this is a god. I know that the Foundation does not approve of using the term, but it is still the case. The Stag is a god, and it is not a petty local god. It is not one of the mild gods of Earth, or some weaker spirit that is bound by the strength of man\u2019s belief.<br /> <br /> We have, for the time being, fooled it into thinking that we have overpowered it. It does not understand that we do so falsely: it is a god. For gods, words have Power. Ritual and belief hold greater power over a god than all the laws of science. </div> </div> </div>I find the idea of beings so powerful and bigger in scale than all of humanity that our laws of nature mean nothing to them a lot scarier than &quot;there is some principle behind it that I can understand in my own terms and use against it&quot;. But to each his own. Trying to figure out the one weak spot of an eldritch monster with the combined efforts of the Mysterium and the Null Mysteriis sounds like a fun idea. Even if they figure out how to stop the monster, they probably won't know exactly the why or how. And curiosity is right up there with hubris in the top 10 reasons that Mages and other investigative types get killed or worse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 11-25-2015, 12:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T09:54:46-08:00","id":774078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774066#post774066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. Which the new &quot;totally-not-an-alloy&quot; maker is co-opting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me see if I can explain why this is a laughably shallow read:<br /> <br /> In Mage, the curses of Proximus lineages can mutate in response to attempts to subvert the spirit of their being a drawback, and the Acanthus-aligned example has already done so on at least one occasion.<br /> <br /> In Demon, the God-Machine's projects often rely on convergences that only work when variables align that are not always concrete \u2014 the Clockwork Man specifically requires that its creator be obsessed with completing it, and the Machine's many gears include literal gears that can be lubricated by either oil or blood.<br /> <br /> In Changeling, <i>you can buy and trade abstractions and the laws of reality change on a regular basis in the parts of the game's cosmology that are not &quot;Earth as experienced by the wakeful.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> When you can mass-produce the universal bane of a race of gods who run on narrative, you render that bane insignificant and so it narrows in focus to compensate. The World of Darkness, while humanocentric, is not a HFY setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T09:56:24-08:00","id":774079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774062#post774062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Immaterial things interact with the world of darkness all the time. There's no guarantee a Fae's anything would have a chemical composition. Sure, in real life, you take a drop of water, divide it down and eventually get your molecule and can even divide that down to its component atoms. But a true fae could just be a drop of water, and you divide that down and just get smaller drops of water, without any sign of molecules or atoms. And yes, at that point you can say that it isn't water, or at least isn't h2o but you can drink it and it sustains you, you can freeze it and it turns to ice, you can boil it and it turns to steam, and you can give it back to the True Fae it came from but it doesn't matter because she grew more.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It's not just the name, it's the concept behind it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Almost everything is an alloy of something, you know. There will always be impurities except in minute quantities. However, it is clealry stated in the book that &quot;impurities&quot; have essentially no baring on the effectiveness of &quot;cold iron.&quot; You can take a chunk of impure iron ore, and it'll still be <b>super effective</b> against Fae. One wonders why we don't just develop Railguns or Coilguns that fire Iron Ore Pellets, or grind down some iron ore and turn it into a spray-based or dust-based weapon.<br /> <br /> Also those &quot;immaterial things&quot; are actually made of stuff. It's called &quot;<b>Ephemeral Matter</b>.&quot; Why the True Fae are some how made of non-existing matter that somehow interacts with the world for no possible explainable reason makes little sense. They're there, they're made of something, so that something is a something, we just don't know what that something is. Yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T09:56:31-08:00","id":774080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774073#post774073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if they figure out how to stop the monster, they probably won't know exactly the why or how.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is more or less fine; we don't know <i>why</i> about of fair number of things, just that they <i>do</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774073#post774073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And curiosity is right up there with hubris in the top 10 reasons that Mages and other investigative types get killed or worse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Before or after tenticles?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774078#post774078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When you can mass-produce the universal bane of a race of gods who run on narrative, you render that bane insignificant and so it narrows in focus to compensate. The World of Darkness, while humanocentric, is not a HFY setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>One can also interpret it as, through cunning and wisdom, stealing the secret of said gods weakness from the jaws of reality.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774079#post774079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also those &quot;immaterial things&quot; are actually made of stuff. It's called &quot;<b>Ephemeral Matter</b>.&quot; Why the True Fae are some how made of non-existing matter that somehow interacts with the world for no possible explainable reason makes little sense. They're there, they're made of something, so that something is a something, we just don't know what that something is. Yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wasn't one of the reasons the True Fae were weaker in the &quot;real&quot; world, due to them having to play ball with said world's rules more than they are used to, or might like? (Granted, that may not be kept going into 2ed)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 11-25-2015, 01:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T10:02:31-08:00","id":774084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774079#post774079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Almost everything is an alloy of something, you know. There will always be impurities except in minute quantities. However, it is clealry stated in the book that &quot;impurities&quot; have essentially no baring on the effectiveness of &quot;cold iron.&quot; You can take a chunk of impure iron ore, and it'll still be <b>super effective</b> against Fae. One wonders why we don't just develop Railguns or Coilguns that fire Iron Ore Pellets, or grind down some iron ore and turn it into a spray-based or dust-based weapon.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's the fact that people don't believe in True Fae, even if you explain them in detail and hand them a core book you traded your smile for at the local goblin market.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also those &quot;immaterial things&quot; are actually made of stuff. It's called &quot;<b>Ephemeral Matter</b>.&quot; Why the True Fae are some how made of non-existing matter that somehow interacts with the world for no possible explainable reason makes little sense. They're there, they're made of something, so that something is a something, we just don't know what that something is. Yet. </div> </div> </div>Ephemeral beings are not the only things in the World of Darkness. Strix are made of darkness. They are not ephemeral. A strix can enter a vampire, drain the blood out of three humans, turn it to Vitae, then leave the vampire and be the same blot of shadow with three peoples worth of Vitae in it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T10:09:10-08:00","id":774090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774084#post774084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's the fact that people don't believe in True Fae, even if you explain them in detail and hand them a core book you traded your smile for at the local goblin market.<br /> <br /> Ephemeral beings are not the only things in the World of Darkness. Strix are made of darkness. They are not ephemeral. A strix can enter a vampire, drain the blood out of three humans, turn it to Vitae, then leave the vampire and be the same blot of shadow with three peoples worth of Vitae in it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that it's not &quot;Darkness&quot; as the absence of light, but &quot;Darkness&quot; as a form of tangible matter (Like Dark Matter). It's the same word for two <b>entirely different things</b>.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774073#post774073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find the idea of beings so powerful and bigger in scale than all of humanity that our laws of nature mean nothing to them a lot scarier than &quot;there is some principle behind it that I can understand in my own terms and use against it&quot;. But to each his own. Trying to figure out the one weak spot of an eldritch monster with the combined efforts of the Mysterium and the Null Mysteriis sounds like a fun idea. Even if they figure out how to stop the monster, they probably won't know exactly the why or how. And curiosity is right up there with hubris in the top 10 reasons that Mages and other investigative types get killed or worse.</div> </div> </div> </div>The catch is &quot;according to our understanding of chemistry and biology&quot; which is of course constantly changing and evolving while we, as a species, learn more and catalog it for the newer generations. If you've ever tried to learn about Quantum Mechanics you might well consider it far beyond your understanding. But that's why we have scientists that spend many years of their life learning how it works and how to dilute it down into a form that the masses can understand. I do not see how magic, fairy dust, etc. cannot function the same way. I'm not a believer in &quot;<a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/StatusQuoIsGod\" target=\"_blank\">The Status Quo is God</a>&quot; The reason why it exists in the game is because the game is supposed to always have the same starting point. Though of course you can have storytellers run games that have a chronology and actually go places.<br /> <br /> The only reason why Investigative types tend to die is because the world's supposed to be a scary place, and if you illuminate everything and make it make sense then it's less scary. Obviously the God-Machine wants none of that, because it exists to enforce the status quo. <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/HeKnowsTooMuch\" target=\"_blank\">So accidents may happen</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","user":"ReshyShira","date":". 11-25-2015, 01:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T10:23:53-08:00","id":774094,"title":"","content":"The Fae <i>do</i> follow a well-defined set of rules. The problem is that to understand them you need a lawyer, not a physicist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T10:25:39-08:00","id":774095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774094#post774094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Fae <i>do</i> follow a well-defined set of rules. The problem is that to understand them you need a lawyer, not a physicist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not both? Furthermore, what prevents it from being understood, put on paper, and then being distilled into a form of information that the masses can understand?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T10:26:47-08:00","id":774096,"title":"","content":"The word for &quot;ephemeral matter&quot; is actually &quot;ephemera&quot;, and Strix are not made of ephemera. What they're made from is darkness given independent form, which is more comparable to smoke than dark matter. If they were made of dark matter they would be impossible to see, since dark matter doesn't interact with any normal matter, including photons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T10:26:56-08:00","id":774097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774090#post774090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except that it's not &quot;Darkness&quot; as the absence of light, but &quot;Darkness&quot; as a form of tangible matter (Like Dark Matter).</div> </div> </div> </div>Except it's not tangible. That's why they're immune to physical or ephemeral attacks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774095#post774095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why not both? Furthermore, what prevents it from being understood, put on paper, and then being distilled into a form of information that the masses can understand?</div> </div> </div> </div>Arguably the same thing preventing you from understanding what we're trying to get across. It doesn't work off of your paradigm. The story of iron is what matters to the Fae, not its chemical composition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-25-2015, 01:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T10:30:12-08:00","id":774100,"title":"","content":"Strix <i>are</i> tangible, they're just gaseous. You can trap one in a jar just fine. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774095#post774095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why not both? Furthermore, what prevents it from being understood, put on paper, and then being distilled into a form of information that the masses can understand?</div> </div> </div> </div>Paragraph 14, subsection b.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T10:30:47-08:00","id":774101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774095#post774095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why not both? Furthermore, what prevents it from being understood, put on paper, and then being distilled into a form of information that the masses can understand?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, isn't that kind of what the Game of Immortals from Equinox Road is?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T10:35:38-08:00","id":774103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774100#post774100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Strix <i>are</i> tangible, they're just gaseous. You can trap one in a jar just fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>And some of them can break out of that jar just fine, and all of them can talk directly to your mind simply by making-eye contact, even if that jar is soundproofed somehow. But I suppose semi-tangible would fit. They can turn into smoke, but they can also turn into shadow, I wouldn't say they were always gaseous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T10:45:22-08:00","id":774110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774100#post774100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Strix <i>are</i> tangible, they're just gaseous. You can trap one in a jar just fine.<br /> <br /> Paragraph 14, subsection b.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/DramaticallyMissingThePoint\" target=\"_blank\">If I knew what book you were talking about, I'd probably go and look it up. </a><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774097#post774097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except it's not tangible. That's why they're immune to physical or ephemeral attacks.<br /> <br /> Arguably the same thing preventing you from understanding what we're trying to get across. It doesn't work off of your paradigm. The story of iron is what matters to the Fae, not its chemical composition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/ClapYourHandsIfYouBelieve\" target=\"_blank\">reality by concensus</a>, if you made your own story and it was popular enough (say a book), then wouldn't whatever that material is gain effectiveness against Fae? Furthermore, if you destroyed any knowledge of Fae would they then disappear, having no longer any stories on them to base their powers (or vulnerabilities)?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774096#post774096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The word for &quot;ephemeral matter&quot; is actually &quot;ephemera&quot;, and Strix are not made of ephemera. What they're made from is darkness given independent form, which is more comparable to smoke than dark matter. If they were made of dark matter they would be impossible to see, since dark matter doesn't interact with any normal matter, including photons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that dark matter does interact with things? It has a gravitational pull, for instance. <a href=\"http://www.forbes.com/sites/startswithabang/2015/11/24/strange-but-true-dark-matter-grows-hair-around-stars-and-planets/\" target=\"_blank\">Heck, it supposedly grows &quot;hair&quot; around planets.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774103#post774103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And some of them can break out of that jar just fine, and all of them can talk directly to your mind simply by making-eye contact, even if that jar is soundproofed somehow. But I suppose semi-tangible would fit. They can turn into smoke, but they can also turn into shadow, I wouldn't say they were always gaseous.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're &quot;Shadows&quot; and &quot;Darkness&quot; with quotation marks, as they are not the same shadows as those we see in our daily lives, possessing entirely different properties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T10:53:29-08:00","id":774122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774110#post774110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/ClapYourHandsIfYouBelieve\" target=\"_blank\">reality by concensus</a>, if you made your own story and it was popular enough (say a book), then wouldn't whatever that material is gain effectiveness against Fae? \\</div> </div> </div> </div>If the Fae in question was based on the story from your book then this would likely work. This is how Changelings escape Arcadia, by taking advantage of the narrative rules the Fae have enforced upon themselves based on the stories they represent. It WOULDN'T work on ALL Fae.<br /> <br /> Ignoring the inspirations for the Fae (Folklore tales); in World of Darkness terms, the Fae are weak to Iron, the concept, not the material. Narrative is more important than reality in Changeling (as a metaphysical facet of the Faes' existence).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T10:54:12-08:00","id":774123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774110#post774110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sounds like <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/ClapYourHandsIfYouBelieve\" target=\"_blank\">reality by concensus</a>, if you made your own story and it was popular enough (say a book), then wouldn't whatever that material is gain effectiveness against Fae? Furthermore, if you destroyed any knowledge of Fae would they then disappear, having no longer any stories on them to base their powers (or vulnerabilities)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that is explicitly how the fae work. Although any such attempt to do so would be met by absolutely tremendous resistance from nigh-godlike beings, which is a large part of the reason it hasn't happened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T10:57:51-08:00","id":774126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774110#post774110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/ClapYourHandsIfYouBelieve\" target=\"_blank\">reality by concensus</a>, if you made your own story and it was popular enough (say a book), then wouldn't whatever that material is gain effectiveness against Fae?</div> </div> </div> </div>Now who's dramatically missing the point? Pretty much the entirety of the game is based in the supernatural. By definition this means things work beyond the laws of nature, and that are not bound by the laws of the natural world. 1+1 doesn't have to equal 2 in the World of Darkness. Some things may work on more understandable rules, but that's often because they are more bound to certain concepts. A werewolf, for instance, is going to be especially wounded by pure silver in any form. As we've pointed out several times, it doesn't matter how pure the iron content is in your steel, it won't have a special effect on a true fae.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Furthermore, if you destroyed any knowledge of Fae would they then disappear, having no longer any stories on them to base their powers (or vulnerabilities)? </div> </div> </div>There's some belief that if every story was erased or every human dead, the Fae might no longer exist. But there's some evidence pointing to the idea that they existed long before humanity and will exist long after.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They're &quot;Shadows&quot; and &quot;Darkness&quot; with quotation marks, as they are not the same shadows as those we see in our daily lives, possessing entirely different properties. </div> </div> </div>Yes. The shadows we see in our daily lives do not move of their own accord and drink the breath from people. But in the world of darkness, that's what the strix do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T11:01:21-08:00","id":774130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774122#post774122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ignoring the inspirations for the Fae (Folklore tales); in World of Darkness terms, the Fae are weak to Iron, the concept, not the material. Narrative is more important than reality in Changeling (as a metaphysical facet of the Faes' existence).</div> </div> </div> </div>So, again, once you isolate the concept of iron, it doesn't matter whether it is made out of tin, it's &quot;good enough&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T11:02:43-08:00","id":774131,"title":"","content":"The Fae treat time as a suggestion at best, so they will likely exist for as long as humanity has ever believed in them at any point in history.<br /> <br /> So it would take Archmaster-tier reality writing to get rid of them. Which they would be able to resist, being on the same level.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774130#post774130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, again, once you isolate the concept of iron, it doesn't matter whether it is made out of tin, it's &quot;good enough&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you fill a tin object with the concept of iron, it's iron. Although the only place you could potentially do that sort of thing is at a goblin market, and they probably have an embargo on Iron goods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 11-25-2015, 02:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T11:04:24-08:00","id":774133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774110#post774110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except that dark matter does interact with things? It has a gravitational pull, for instance<br /> <a href=\"http://www.forbes.com/sites/startswithabang/2015/11/24/strange-but-true-dark-matter-grows-hair-around-stars-and-planets/\" target=\"_blank\">Heck, it supposedly grows &quot;hair&quot; around planets.</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Gravity is an interaction with <i>spacetime</i>, not an interaction with matter. The article you linked even explicitly calls dark matter collisionless. That's why we can't normally see it and why it can't possibly be what Strix are made of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 11-25-2015, 02:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T11:06:16-08:00","id":774134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774122#post774122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If the Fae in question was based on the story from your book then this would likely work. This is how Changelings escape Arcadia, by taking advantage of the narrative rules the Fae have enforced upon themselves based on the stories they represent. It WOULDN'T work on ALL Fae.<br /> <br /> Ignoring the inspirations for the Fae (Folklore tales); in World of Darkness terms, the Fae are weak to Iron, the concept, not the material. Narrative is more important than reality in Changeling (as a metaphysical facet of the Faes' existence).</div> </div> </div> </div>What exactly is the &quot;concept&quot; of iron that is incompatible with &quot;steel&quot;?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774126#post774126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now who's dramatically missing the point? Pretty much the entirety of the game is based in the supernatural. By definition this means things work beyond the laws of nature, and that are not bound by the laws of the natural world. 1+1 doesn't have to equal 2 in the World of Darkness. Some things may work on more understandable rules, but that's often because they are more bound to certain concepts. A werewolf, for instance, is going to be especially wounded by pure silver in any form. As we've pointed out several times, it doesn't matter how pure the iron content is in your steel, it won't have a special effect on a true fae.<br /> <br /> There's some belief that if every story was erased or every human dead, the Fae might no longer exist. But there's some evidence pointing to the idea that they existed long before humanity and will exist long after.<br /> <br /> Yes. The shadows we see in our daily lives do not move of their own accord and drink the breath from people. But in the world of darkness, that's what the strix do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm so glad you read the links. lol.<br /> <br /> They work beyond the laws of nature as we know them, but as you probably are <b>well aware</b> they follow their laws, despite being supposedly <b>utterly chaotic</b>. If you understand their laws, how they are formed, the implications thereof, and restrictions therein, then you can understand and define how they work. Once you can define how they work, you can start fitting them into the framework of the laws of nature as we know it. Science isn't static, it is ever changing (much like the Fae).<br /> <br /> If you figure out what exactly the properties are that makes &quot;Iron&quot; effective against Fae, then you can formulate it and catalog it in such a manner that it become seasily accessible and well understood. The reason I get after the development team is simply because they failed to even provide consistency within their own source material, which as a game that runs on rules (just like the Fae) it's a demerit towards the integrity of the game.<br /> <br /> The Fae require humans in order to survive (Glamour requirements) so they couldn't have existed before then unless there was another species out there that could provide their Glamour needs.<br /> <br /> The Strix <b>look like</b> shadows but they are not shadows. You're confusing calling someone &quot;Black&quot; and the color &quot;#000000&quot; Both of these are called black, but they represent different things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T11:16:26-08:00","id":774143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774134#post774134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They work beyond the laws of nature as we know them, but as you probably are <b>well aware</b> they follow their laws, despite being supposedly <b>utterly chaotic</b>. If you understand their laws, how they are formed, the implications thereof, and restrictions therein, then you can understand and define how they work. Once you can define how they work, you can start fitting them into the framework of the laws of nature as we know it. Science isn't static, it is ever changing (much like the Fae).</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that's not supernatural. That's natural. By being supernatural they, again, exist beyond the rules of the natural world. Not the laws of nature as we know them, the laws of nature altogether. Their own laws are chaotic, and they define how they work, but they won't fit in the framework of the laws of nature.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you figure out what exactly the properties are that makes &quot;Iron&quot; effective against Fae, then you can formulate it and catalog it in such a manner that it become seasily accessible and well understood. The reason I get after the development team is simply because they failed to even provide consistency within their own source material, which as a game that runs on rules (just like the Fae) it's a demerit towards the integrity of the game. </div> </div> </div>You posted the properties in the first place. Iron, forged by human and hammer, without machine or magic. The books seem fairly consistent on this. Any iron is capable of breaking through fae magic defenses, but only 'cold' iron is capable of doing aggravated damage to True Fae.<br /> <br /> As the book itself points out, 'cold iron is a mythic vulnerability of the fae, and just as the fae themselves, myths are largely unconcerned with science. The folklore and the magic matter, not the hard numbers.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T11:32:23-08:00","id":774152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774143#post774143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except that's not supernatural. That's natural. By being supernatural they, again, exist beyond the rules of the natural world. Not the laws of nature as we know them, the laws of nature altogether. Their own laws are chaotic, and they define how they work, but they won't fit in the framework of the laws of nature.<br /> <br /> You posted the properties in the first place. Iron, forged by human and hammer, without machine or magic. The books seem fairly consistent on this. Any iron is capable of breaking through fae magic defenses, but only 'cold' iron is capable of doing aggravated damage to True Fae.<br /> <br /> As the book itself points out, 'cold iron is a mythic vulnerability of the fae, and just as the fae themselves, myths are largely unconcerned with science. The folklore and the magic matter, not the hard numbers.'</div> </div> </div> </div>Supernatural just means either one of two things. Either it does not exist, or it is not yet explained why it works. It's kind of why &quot;Alternative Medicine&quot; is a sham, because if it worked it'd just be called &quot;Medicine.&quot; We used to not understand diseases, but we had supernatural beliefs about burning bodies. Now we know why burning bodies works, and now it's no longer supernatural. Supernatural is just a term for the unexplained or the false. If their laws were truly unable to understood, then how can you play a changeling? Natural laws only define what we currently understand, so if Fae existed they'd be incorporated into our understanding, thus becoming &quot;natural.&quot;<br /> <br /> And no it's not consistent, Wrought Iron isn't cold iron as it has been smelted and (likely) shaped with machines.<br /> <br /> Also I'm fairly certain if you had a True Fae captive and held in a helpless state you could experiement on them to see what works and what does not, getting observations. Then you could start formulating why it is that this works and that does not, or a hypothesis. Then you'd test out your hypothesis (and others would as well) and see if it fits the framework of your new observations. If it works then it can become a theory, a well substantiated explanation for our observations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T11:48:27-08:00","id":774168,"title":"","content":"The issue is, the &quot;rules&quot; that govern the Fae are themselves inconsistent. You could understand the processes by which they are bound only so long as those laws remained consistent. If your findings can't be reliably reproduced, they cannot become a scientific law.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T11:48:27-08:00","id":774169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774152#post774152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Supernatural just means either one of two things. Either it does not exist, or it is not yet explained why it works. It's kind of why &quot;Alternative Medicine&quot; is a sham, because if it worked it'd just be called &quot;Medicine.&quot; We used to not understand diseases, but we had supernatural beliefs about burning bodies. Now we know why burning bodies works, and now it's no longer supernatural. Supernatural is just a term for the unexplained or the false. If their laws were truly unable to understood, then how can you play a changeling? Natural laws only define what we currently understand, so if Fae existed they'd be incorporated into our understanding, thus becoming &quot;natural.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, that's not supernatural.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And no it's not consistent, Wrought Iron isn't cold iron as it has been smelted and (likely) shaped with machines. </div> </div> </div>And wrought iron doesn't inflict aggravated damage to True Fae, it just goes through fae defenses like most iron.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also I'm fairly certain if you had a True Fae captive and held in a helpless state you could experiement on them to see what works and what does not, getting observations. Then you could start formulating why it is that this works and that does not, or a hypothesis. Then you'd test out your hypothesis (and others would as well) and see if it fits the framework of your new observations. If it works then it can become a theory, a well substantiated explanation for our observations. </div> </div> </div>Okay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T13:21:39-08:00","id":774229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774169#post774169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Again, that's not supernatural.<br /> <br /> And wrought iron doesn't inflict aggravated damage to True Fae, it just goes through fae defenses like most iron.<br /> <br /> Okay.</div> </div> </div> </div>The second you know any facts or information about something it ceases to be supernatural, just like Disease, Poison, Parasites, Fire, Electricity, Acids, Bases, etc. etc. etc. The list goes on and on. Supernatural is a label we apply to things that we do not understand terribly well (or might not be real). The Fae are real, so while we may not understand them well, enough to call them supernatural even, that doesn't mean they are eternally unknowable. It simply means that we don't know about them <b>yet</b>.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774168#post774168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The issue is, the &quot;rules&quot; that govern the Fae are themselves inconsistent. You could understand the processes by which they are bound only so long as those laws remained consistent. If your findings can't be reliably reproduced, they cannot become a scientific law.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? From what I know there are certain traits, facts, and observations we can know about the True Fae. They emulate our folklore, they are vulnerable to certain compositions of iron, they all possess some unusual vulnerabilities called &quot;Frailties,&quot; they seem to be able to alter the world through the use of &quot;contracts&quot; with beings or forces of nature, they all hail from a plane called &quot;Arcadia,&quot; etc. These are all documented within the game's sourcebooks, so how are all of these rules fundamentally inconsistent <b>in all cases all of the time</b>? If they were truly unknowable and impossible to understand, then you couldn't write <b>anything</b> down about them. Except you can, so that's clearly not right.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: I feel like a mage trying to explain how magic works to a sleeper.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T13:42:53-08:00","id":774246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774229#post774229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The second you know any facts or information about something it ceases to be supernatural, just like Disease, Poison, Parasites, Fire, Electricity, Acids, Bases, etc. etc. etc. The list goes on and on. Supernatural is a label we apply to things that we do not understand terribly well (or might not be real). The Fae are real, so while we may not understand them well, enough to call them supernatural even, that doesn't mean they are eternally unknowable. It simply means that we don't know about them <b>yet</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, that's how it works in the real world, that's not how it works in the World of Darkness though. Things exist that <b>CANNOT</b> be explained, period, end of story.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774229#post774229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really? From what I know there are certain traits, facts, and observations we can know about the True Fae. They emulate our folklore, they are vulnerable to certain compositions of iron, they all possess some unusual vulnerabilities called &quot;Frailties,&quot; they seem to be able to alter the world through the use of &quot;contracts&quot; with beings or forces of nature, they all hail from a plane called &quot;Arcadia,&quot; etc. These are all documented within the game's sourcebooks, so how are all of these rules fundamentally inconsistent <b>in all cases all of the time</b>? If they were truly unknowable and impossible to understand, then you couldn't write <b>anything</b> down about them. Except you can, so that's clearly not right.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The sourcebooks exist in this world, not in the World of Darkness, these things are not hard rules in universe, characters don't know that all Fae have Frailties, only that some things work against them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774229#post774229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> EDIT: I feel like a mage trying to explain how magic works to a sleeper.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like a Changeling explaining Fae to a mortal scientist.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T13:52:09-08:00","id":774252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774035#post774035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Obviously the True Fae are based off out folk lore, which usually has Iron as a way to ward them off. Somehow though, White Wolf decided to focus on the &amp;quot;Cold&amp;quot; rather than the &amp;quot;Iron&amp;quot; part. I'm fairly certain if you imprisoned a Fae and cut off it's hand it'd have a chemical composition, it might be a foreign element but it exists. Who knows, maybe the True Fae are some kind of Silicon Lifeform. Suffice to say though, they exist so they're made of something. Whatever that something is. If they were immaterial then they couldn't interact with the world. They can, so they're obviously material in some degree.<br /> <br /> On the &amp;quot;Steel&amp;quot; is &amp;quot;Steel&amp;quot; thing I don't see why it matters what it's called. It's still made of iron, and steel can be Cold-Worked. If your thought is &amp;quot;Well names do matter&amp;quot; then make some slightly different composition alloy that's primarily made of iron and call it iron, bam done.<br /> <br /> Fire is not acceptable, it even says so. If it's been &amp;quot;heated&amp;quot; it's not &amp;quot;cold iron&amp;quot; according to the book. But somehow, Meteorites are still &amp;quot;Cold Iron&amp;quot; for no explained reason..</div> </div> </div> </div>Most people outside of artisans don't realize it but cold-wrought or cold-forged iron actual refers to cold quenching the &quot;iron&quot; by dipping the red hot metal in water, snow or ice. Moreover, this is a method for making steel, and specifically or especially steel swords.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T13:52:21-08:00","id":774254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774246#post774246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, that's how it works in the real world, that's not how it works in the World of Darkness though. Things exist that <b>CANNOT</b> be explained, period, end of story.<br /> <br /> The sourcebooks exist in this world, not in the World of Darkness, these things are not hard rules in universe, characters don't know that all Fae have Frailties, only that some things work against them.<br /> <br /> I feel like a Changeling explaining Fae to a mortal scientist.</div> </div> </div> </div>So what you are telling me is that in World of Darkness, you cannot learn anything. Thing that exist cannot be learned about, known, or even understood to even the smallest of capacity. Lycanthropes might be balloons, kittens, bipedal wolfmen, glowing balls of light, or rocks; I mean who the hell knows?<br /> <br /> World of Darkness has source books that give how things are supposed to work, obviously the Storyteller can change those rules; but that's because it's a fantasy setting up to the interpretation and whim of someone trying to tell a story. It's fictional, obviously. You may not know that Fae have frailties, but they do; that's an objective fact presented in the rulebook. there may be outliers, but as a general rule they have those vulnerabilities.<br /> <br /> You're a changeling telling a mortal scientist that they couldn't possibly understand. No explanation is happening, just assertions of non-understanding. &quot;You couldn't possible understand.&quot; &quot;Try me.&quot; &quot;No, you really couldn't understand.&quot; &quot;I'm fairly certain I could.&quot; etc.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I don't mean to come off as aggressive, mind. I realize I am overusing personal language, so I apologize for that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774252#post774252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Most people outside of artisans don't realize it but cold-wrought or cold-forged iron actual refers to cold quenching the &quot;iron&quot; by dipping the red hot metal in water, snow or ice. Moreover, this is a method for making steel, and specifically or especially steel swords.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's interesting, I'd really like to see it reflected in the mechanics of the game. I'm not a metalworker so I wouldn't know all the details of metallurgy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","user":"ReshyShira","date":". 11-25-2015, 05:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T14:14:03-08:00","id":774275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774254#post774254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So what you are telling me is that in World of Darkness, you cannot learn anything. Thing that exist cannot be learned about, known, or even understood to even the smallest of capacity. Lycanthropes might be balloons, kittens, bipedal wolfmen, glowing balls of light, or rocks; I mean who the hell knows?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>No, I'm saying SOME things cannot be explained, codified or relied upon to be consistent, not everything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774254#post774254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> World of Darkness has source books that give how things are supposed to work, obviously the Storyteller can change those rules; but that's because it's a fantasy setting up to the interpretation and whim of someone trying to tell a story. It's fictional, obviously. You may not know that Fae have frailties, but they do; that's an objective fact presented in the rulebook. there may be outliers, but as a general rule they have those vulnerabilities.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not saying the books can't be clearer on what affects Fae in what ways, I'm saying that it wont be based on the purity of Iron or that something that is purer Iron (such as steel) will count because that is what steel actually is (purer Iron). I'm saying it will be based on the Narrative idea of Iron. Even if that doesn't make any sense from a realistic point of view.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774254#post774254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're a changeling telling a mortal scientist that they couldn't possibly understand. No explanation is happening, just assertions of non-understanding. &quot;You couldn't possible understand.&quot; &quot;Try me.&quot; &quot;No, you really couldn't understand.&quot; &quot;I'm fairly certain I could.&quot; etc.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's like quantifying 'fun', any attempt at explanation is going to sound like that. (And you could totally buy a bottle of fun in a goblin market that would produce fun when opened but there would be nothing in the bottle that can be measured by ANY means).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T14:25:44-08:00","id":774278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774254#post774254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's interesting, I'd really like to see it reflected in the mechanics of the game. I'm not a metalworker so I wouldn't know all the details of metallurgy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's adequately covered by bans and storyteller warrant (aka storyteller makes new bans as necessary).<br /> <br /> Also, I think you may want to dial back your diatribe a bit. All the things you're complaining about are really the storyteller's responsibility and it's not the purpose of the rule books to provide the kinds of rules you seem to want. Even with V:tR 2nd Ed., the bans in the book are examples and not an exhaustive list.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T14:33:11-08:00","id":774283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774275#post774275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I'm saying SOME things cannot be explained, codified or relied upon to be consistent, not everything.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying the books can't be clearer on what affects Fae in what ways, I'm saying that it wont be based on the purity of Iron or that something that is purer Iron (such as steel) will count because that is what steel actually is (purer Iron). I'm saying it will be based on the Narrative idea of Iron. Even if that doesn't make any sense from a realistic point of view.<br /> <br /> It's like quantifying 'fun', any attempt at explanation is going to sound like that. (And you could totally buy a bottle of fun in a goblin market that would produce fun when opened but there would be nothing in the bottle that can be measured by ANY means).</div> </div> </div> </div>If something cannot be explained or understood then it doesn't exist. That's the main catch. <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2w0fInUhtnk\" target=\"_blank\">We cannot understand the Fae, just like we couldn't understand the Solar system, a Round Earth, Disease, Chemistry, etc. etc.</a> This is due to lack of information, lack of knowledge, lack of testing. If you could test, know, or glean information about the Fae then you could understand them. Obviously all Fae are different, but so are all humans. Does that make us completely unknowable? No. We follow patterns and rules, just as the Fae do. Heck, the Fae are measure their power by &quot;Fate.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Thing is that if you can formulate what makes Iron more Iron(y), then you can formulate and replicate it. If it requires so much impurities to be effective, then it can be replicated. I'm fairly certain if you had a variety of different knives of different make (Steel, to Stainless Steel, to Iron, to Brass, etc.) you could easily quantify what works and what does not. And in that case you have just analyzed magic.<br /> <br /> <br /> It's hard to quantify &quot;Fun&quot; because the brain and the psyche is still not well understood. I'm fairly certain in the next few centuries we'll have probably figured out what makes an activity fun and stimulating. Science is constantly marching on, steadily refining and increasing our understanding of the world. Short baby steps, but progress is being made every day.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774278#post774278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that's adequately covered by bans and storyteller warrant (aka storyteller makes new bans as necessary).<br /> <br /> Also, I think you may want to dial back your diatribe a bit. All the things you're complaining about are really the storyteller's responsibility and it's not the purpose of the rule books to provide the kinds of rules you seem to want. Even with V:tR 2nd Ed., the bans in the book are examples and not an exhaustive list.</div> </div> </div> </div>I realize I'm not terribly diplomatic, it's a pretty big character flaw of mine. I'm bad at explaining things as well. I do understand that some things are left to the storyteller, but in the case of Cold Iron I'd really like concrete answers because it's kind of important for running a changeling game. I don't generally like murkiness in games, especially when it comes to important details like what bypasses the players and True Fae's resistances.<br /> <br /> I don't know how to really explain it, it's like saying it's vulnerable to fire, but only fire not made by human hands and doesn't actually cause or result in the burning of material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","user":"ReshyShira","date":". 11-25-2015, 05:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T14:53:43-08:00","id":774288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774283#post774283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If something cannot be explained or understood then it doesn't exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's inaccurate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We cannot understand the Fae, just like we couldn't understand the Solar system, a Round Earth, Disease, Chemistry, etc. etc. </div> </div> </div>And they all existed without people's understanding of them, though they learned to explain most of it later. But the Fae, like the Abyss and many other things in the World of Darkness, are supernatural. They exist. They can be explained to a degree, and understood to a degree, but they are ultimately unknowable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you could test, know, or glean information about the Fae then you could understand them. Obviously all Fae are different, but so are all humans. Does that make us completely unknowable? No. We follow patterns and rules, just as the Fae do. Heck, the Fae are measure their power by &quot;Fate.&quot; </div> </div> </div>You keep comparing the supernatural to the natural, and in this you miss the entire point of the concept of supernatural.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thing is that if you can formulate what makes Iron more Iron(y), then you can formulate and replicate it. If it requires so much impurities to be effective, then it can be replicated. I'm fairly certain if you had a variety of different knives of different make (Steel, to Stainless Steel, to Iron, to Brass, etc.) you could easily quantify what works and what does not. And in that case you have just analyzed magic. </div> </div> </div>We've said this, several times. Being 'more irony' doesn't make iron any more or less effective against true fae. You've already quantified what works and what does not. Hand forged, no fire, no machines, no magic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm bad at explaining things as well. I do understand that some things are left to the storyteller, but in the case of Cold Iron I'd really like concrete answers because it's kind of important for running a changeling game. I don't generally like murkiness in games, especially when it comes to important details like what bypasses the players and True Fae's resistances. </div> </div> </div>You're explaining your side just fine, but you're limiting yourself by forcing the supernatural to work via natural laws. Square peg in round hole, and when others explain to you that the square peg is a square peg and doesn't belong in a round hole, you seem to think if you just turn it the right way, it will fit smoothly in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't know how to really explain it, it's like saying it's vulnerable to fire, but only fire not made by human hands and doesn't actually cause or result in the burning of material. </div> </div> </div>That's how some bans work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T15:14:39-08:00","id":774300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774288#post774288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's inaccurate.<br /> <br /> And they all existed without people's understanding of them, though they learned to explain most of it later. But the Fae, like the Abyss and many other things in the World of Darkness, are supernatural. They exist. They can be explained to a degree, and understood to a degree, but they are ultimately unknowable.<br /> <br /> You keep comparing the supernatural to the natural, and in this you miss the entire point of the concept of supernatural.<br /> <br /> We've said this, several times. Being 'more irony' doesn't make iron any more or less effective against true fae. You've already quantified what works and what does not. Hand forged, no fire, no machines, no magic.<br /> <br /> You're explaining your side just fine, but you're limiting yourself by forcing the supernatural to work via natural laws. Square peg in round hole, and when others explain to you that the square peg is a square peg and doesn't belong in a round hole, you seem to think if you just turn it the right way, it will fit smoothly in.<br /> <br /> That's how some bans work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Supernatural is something that cannot be explained by nature <b>as we know it</b>, that does not mean that our world view cannot <b>expand to answer them</b>. If they are utterly unknowable, then it would be impossible for anyone (changeling, human, mage, lycanthrope, etc.) to possess knowledge that they even exist. Yet some (not necessarily that many) know they exist. Since they are known to exist then they're able to be learned about. I don't see why this is a hard concept to grasp. Everything supernatural up to this point in the history of history as we know it has been one of two things. Either the supernatural is something that has (historically) not been well understood, or has been a falsehood due to humanities capability to find false positives and false negatives in things.<br /> <br /> If the Square peg doesn't fit the round hole, then we change the hole so that the peg will fit and make sense with the rest of the picture. That's because we <b>learn</b>, we <b>adapt</b>, we <b>grow</b> in our understanding of the world around us. Saying that something is eternally beyond our grasp means that a Mage couldn't see magic, use magic, conceive of magic, etc. Yet they quite clearly can see through the Lie. Same goes for changelings, lycanthropes, geists, protheans, etc. They can understand it, they can learn about it; more over <b>they can learn about each other</b>; might seem alien to the great unwashed but it <b>can be understood</b>. Nothing prevents a Lycanthrope, Changeling, Mage, etc. from writing what they know or understand on paper.<br /> <br /> <br /> On the issue of Bans, the issue I see is that it seems to be trying to be both literal, and allegory simultaneously.<a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/ClapYourHandsIfYouBelieve\" target=\"_blank\"> If it was a case of the faith in the weapon gives it power (Hence why a weapon you're told has been tempered under the blood moon of the 5th year of the century in the arctic tends to work better than one you know is mass produced) that'd be perfectly fine and I'd have no problems with it (after all, all humans supposedly have the potential to be mages).</a> Except this isn't the case, because there's literal examples that destroy any potential allegory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","user":"ReshyShira","date":". 11-25-2015, 06:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T15:28:30-08:00","id":774318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774288#post774288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You've already quantified what works and what does not. Hand forged, no fire, no machines, no magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>So it's completely knowable and replicable......<br /> <br /> Also, it is impossible to have something unknowable, despite it being perfectly possible for something to exist that we might never understand. For x to exist, y must have happened to cause x. It just may be that we don't possess the knowledge to figureout the link between x and y because our brains are designed to see specific sorts of patterns, and Gentry operate under different laws, but they still have to operate under laws. We know they do follow laws through things like their weakness to Cold Iron, it just happens that it doesn't have to do with conditions a, b, or c like humans would expect it matters on whether it's impacted by the contract that was made that caused the Cold Iron to be harmful. The contract become scientific laws with Gentry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 11-25-2015, 06:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T15:32:37-08:00","id":774322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774300#post774300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Supernatural is something that cannot be explained by nature <b>as we know it</b>, that does not mean that our world view cannot <b>expand to answer them</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Again. Supernatural is something that cannot be explained by natural laws. Period. Full stop. <a href=\"http://www.thefreedictionary.com/supernatural\" target=\"_blank\">Here are several </a><a href=\"http://dictionary.reference.com/browse/supernatural\" target=\"_blank\">dictionaries you can</a> <a href=\"http://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/supernatural\" target=\"_blank\">reference for evidence</a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If they are utterly unknowable, then it would be impossible for anyone (changeling, human, mage, lycanthrope, etc.) to possess knowledge that they even exist. Yet some (not necessarily that many) know they exist. Since they are known to exist then they're able to be learned about. I don't see why this is a hard concept to grasp. </div> </div> </div>They are not utterly unknowable, but most of what they are is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Everything supernatural up to this point in the history of history as we know it has been one of two things. Either the supernatural is something that has (historically) not been well understood, or has been a falsehood due to humanities capability to find false positives and false negatives in things. </div> </div> </div>Yes, in real life. World of Darkness is not real life, and does not follow the real world's rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the Square peg doesn't fit the round hole, then we change the hold so that the peg will fit and make sense with the rest of the picture. That's because we <b>learn</b>, we <b>adapt</b>, we <b>grow</b> in our understanding of the world around us. Saying that something is eternally beyond our grasp means that a Mage couldn't see magic, use magic, conceive of magic, etc. Yet they quite clearly can see through the Lie. Same goes for changelings, lycanthropes, geists, protheans, etc. They can understand it, they can learn about it; more over <b>they can learn about each other</b>; might seem alien to the great unwashed but it <b>can be understood</b>. Nothing prevents a Lycanthrope, Changeling, Mage, etc. from writing what they know or understand on paper. </div> </div> </div>And still, none of them will be able to understand all of it, or even most. They can observe things and make guesses, but just around the corner there's something that breaks the rules and proves their theories wrong.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774318#post774318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it's completely knowable and replicable......</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Iron and its impact on fae magic and the True Fae are one of the things completely knowable and replicable, as I've said several times it was explained in the first post. There's at least one Keeper working on overcoming their weakness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-25-2015, 06:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T15:44:55-08:00","id":774331,"title":"","content":"Well, as far as the supernatural goes in the world of darkness it's not <i>technically</i> supernatural there. It's just a word we use to mean &quot;weird magic shit&quot;. It all has rules and it can be studied. But those rules have <i>nothing to do with physics</i>. Physics is earth's local by-laws. There are a bunch of other worlds that make up the wod verse and they <i>all</i> follow their own, very much real rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T15:50:21-08:00","id":774334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774322#post774322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. Again. Supernatural is something that cannot be explained by natural laws. Period. Full stop. <a href=\"http://www.thefreedictionary.com/supernatural\" target=\"_blank\">Here are several </a><a href=\"http://dictionary.reference.com/browse/supernatural\" target=\"_blank\">dictionaries you can</a> <a href=\"http://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/supernatural\" target=\"_blank\">reference for evidence</a>.<br /> <br /> They are not utterly unknowable, but most of what they are is.<br /> <br /> Yes, in real life. World of Darkness is not real life, and does not follow the real world's rules.<br /> <br /> And still, none of them will be able to understand all of it, or even most. They can observe things and make guesses, but just around the corner there's something that breaks the rules and proves their theories wrong.<br /> <br /> Yes. Iron and its impact on fae magic and the True Fae are one of the things completely knowable and replicable, as I've said several times it was explained in the first post. There's at least one Keeper working on overcoming their weakness.</div> </div> </div> </div> <b>su\u00b7per\u00b7nat\u00b7u\u00b7ral</b><br /> <br /> (so\u035eo\u2032p\u0259r-n\u0103ch\u2032\u0259r-\u0259l) <i>adj.</i> <b>1. </b> Of or relating to existence outside the natural world.<br /> <b>2. </b> Attributed to a power that seems to violate or go beyond natural forces.<br /> <b>3. </b> Of or relating to a deity.<br /> <b>4. </b> Of or relating to the immediate exercise of divine power; miraculous.<br /> <b>5. </b> Of or relating to the miraculous.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Full Definition of <i>supernatural</i></b><ul><li><i>1</i> : of or relating to an order of existence beyond the visible observable universe; <i>especially</i> : of or relating to God or a god, demigod, spirit, or devil</li> <li><i>2</i><i>a</i> : departing from what is usual or normal especially so as to appear to transcend the laws of nature<i>b</i> : attributed to an invisible agent (as a ghost or spirit)</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <br /> Pay keen attention to definition 2, the word &quot;seem&quot; and &quot;appear.&quot; These are the words I am getting at, something is supernatural so long as it is not well understood. Hence why we have Arthur C. Clark's three laws: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>When a distinguished but elderly scientist states that something is possible, he is almost certainly right. When he states that something is impossible, he is very probably wrong.</li> <li>The only way of discovering the limits of the possible is to venture a little way past them into the impossible.</li> <li>Any sufficiently advanced technology is indistinguishable from magic.</li> </ol><br /> This is what I believe should be held to heart. It seems to me there to be a fundamental assumption that because something doesn't appear to fit with what is currently known that it is forever unknown. Imagine if we just gave up on trying to understand the world around us, we'd have no such things like computers, internet, electricity, etc. Why? Because we would have abandoned curiosity and denied any interest in learning. I believe this to be the bane of our existence.<br /> <br /> <br /> And indeed, most of what they are is unknown <b>for now</b>, will they be eternally unknowable? I find that unlikely. Just as we have learned about the world around us I believe that we'd eventually learn about things that violate our current preconceptions of reality. Again, this is mostly posturing, for it is a fictional setting. But I don't really buy that something can be eternally unknowable, as we have yet to find a single example. For if such an example existed, then you couldn't prove it existed for it was unknowable.<br /> <br /> <br /> So because the Mages, Lycanthropes, Changelings, etc. do not know everything they should make <b>no effort to catalog what they know</b> or <b>collaborate with others and what they know</b>? That's an incredibly defeatist attitude.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774331#post774331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, as far as the supernatural goes in the world of darkness it's not <i>technically</i> supernatural there. It's just a word we use to mean &quot;weird magic shit&quot;. It all has rules and it can be studied. But those rules have <i>nothing to do with physics</i>. Physics is earth's local by-laws. There are a bunch of other worlds that make up the wod verse and they <i>all</i> follow their own, very much real rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly, so what prevents us from opening a new field of study like &quot;Lycanthropic Biology&quot; or &quot;Fae Anatomy&quot;? What about &quot;Physics of the Supernal Planes&quot;? Etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T15:55:50-08:00","id":774340,"title":"","content":"&quot;You cut open the Fae's chest and are knocked over by a cloud of fireflies that erupts from the incision.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T15:59:04-08:00","id":774342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774340#post774340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;You cut open the Fae's chest and are knocked over by a cloud of fireflies that erupts from the incision.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Interesting, so if I make another incision do I get the same result? If I cut a different part of the body does something else erupt from the wound instead? Let's find out. Oh, assistant, please make sure to catch all those fireflies, I wish to study them as well.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T16:08:03-08:00","id":774346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774334#post774334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is what I believe should be held to heart.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, like I said, square peg, round hole.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It seems to me there to be a fundamental assumption that because something doesn't appear to fit with what is currently known that it is forever unknown. Imagine if we just gave up on trying to understand the world around us, we'd have no such things like computers, internet, electricity, etc. Why? Because we would have abandoned curiosity and denied any interest in learning. I believe this to be the bane of our existence. </div> </div> </div>And that's fine in the real world, but in the world of darkness, where the darkness is mystery itself, things being unexplainable is practically a law of nature of its own.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, the Fae you're dissecting is an Actor, and anything that results from its dissection is something the True Fae contrived for you while being an ocean of fire the size of a galaxy in Arcadia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T16:16:14-08:00","id":774354,"title":"","content":"Yeah, most of the other stuff you could study. <br /> <br /> The Fae will just fuck with you for giggles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T16:20:32-08:00","id":774359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774346#post774346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, like I said, square peg, round hole.<br /> <br /> And that's fine in the real world, but in the world of darkness, where the darkness is mystery itself, things being unexplainable is practically a law of nature of its own.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, the Fae you're dissecting is an Actor, and anything that results from its dissection is something the True Fae contrived for you while being an ocean of fire the size of a galaxy in Arcadia.</div> </div> </div> </div>So explain to me why humans cannot change their perceptions of reality to absorb new information presented in World of Darkness? Also I understand the narrative need for some things to be unknown, but the players should be able to learn them, it's part of developing a persistent setting. Things progress.<br /> <br /> &quot;So you're telling me that this thing is just a highly advanced Fetch?&quot; Also I will note that I had always thought that the plane of Arcadia itself was alive (Think a Genius Loci, a living location), and that the &quot;True Fae&quot; are just manifestations or constructs of it's power and form. When it makes a changeling &quot;eat&quot; part of itself, it is just parasitizing the human host which will then metastasis into another &quot;organ&quot; of the plane which then is recalled and added to the whole. Freaky alien biology and all that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T16:24:14-08:00","id":774361,"title":"","content":"Yeah, we're having a big disconnect here. ReyshyShira, your views about the way science works is completely accurate in real life. But World of Darkness is fiction, and in fiction, if the author says something is unknowable, it's unknowable. The Fae of the World of Darkness complicate these issues further, because the laws they follow are the laws of narrative fiction. Which are malleable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T16:27:34-08:00","id":774365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774342#post774342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &amp;quot;Interesting, so if I make another incision do I get the same result? If I cut a different part of the body does something else erupt from the wound instead? Let's find out. Oh, assistant, please make sure to catch all those fireflies, I wish to study them as well.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Still not seeing why the rulebook needs to explain this.<br /> <br /> More to point though, what we believe shapes what we accept as evidence. For someone who is a scientist there is a &quot;natural laws&quot; explanation for why sparks fly when you strike flint with steel (it has to do with friction and abrasion). An animist will explain that flint does not like steel very much and becomes an angry rock when struck by flint and that is why the sparks fly. The animist is not wrong. Other animists find his explanation adequate.<br /> <br /> The point of the WoD is magic and mystery. Part of the game experience is for the storytellers and players to jointly develop the kind of explanations you seek.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T16:33:47-08:00","id":774375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774359#post774359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So explain to me why humans cannot change their perceptions of reality to absorb new information presented in World of Darkness?</div> </div> </div> </div>For one thing, the information presented isn't presented in its entirety. As stated before, there are things that contradict other hard-set rules. Basically, if you want to understand the World of Darkness you come at it like a player might. You don't know what's out there, but things will reveal themselves in time, when they do you take advantage and appreciate that there's still more darkness out there. Just be open to ideas, even if they don't make sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also I understand the narrative need for some things to be unknown, but the players should be able to learn them, it's part of developing a persistent setting. Things progress. </div> </div> </div>And the setting fully encourages you to do whatever you want with the players in regards to them understanding the world of darkness. Give them answers, let them quantify it, let them be befuddled constantly, drive them insane, or blast some cosmic horror at them. The setting has managed to be persistent throughout its first edition, for the most part. Being handed down answers wouldn't represent a progression for the game, it would limit the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T17:09:26-08:00","id":774395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774375#post774375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For one thing, the information presented isn't presented in its entirety. As stated before, there are things that contradict other hard-set rules. Basically, if you want to understand the World of Darkness you come at it like a player might. You don't know what's out there, but things will reveal themselves in time, when they do you take advantage and appreciate that there's still more darkness out there. Just be open to ideas, even if they don't make sense.<br /> <br /> And the setting fully encourages you to do whatever you want with the players in regards to them understanding the world of darkness. Give them answers, let them quantify it, let them be befuddled constantly, drive them insane, or blast some cosmic horror at them. The setting has managed to be persistent throughout its first edition, for the most part. Being handed down answers wouldn't represent a progression for the game, it would limit the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing that I have a problem with cold iron is that it's both an answer and a non-answer. It doesn't state for the Storyteller to decide what cold iron is, or give examples of what it could be. Instead it gives an objective definition that ends up only confusing the issue further. That's the main issue I have with it. That's a bad thing. If you want to say that it's limiting to give strict definitions, then why bother defining &quot;Cold Iron&quot; in the first place? The obvious answer is that it is there to provide structure, just as the fluff of the setting is there to provide structure. If the storyteller wants to, they can easily throw out the entire section on &quot;Cold Iron&quot; and make something else up entirely. That's perfectly within their rights to do as a Storyteller. However, the books are supposed to give a consistent, understandable baseline and I do not believe that the entry on &quot;Cold Iron&quot; really clarifies anything or gives a concrete foundation for Storytellers to build off of. It just seems to confuse the issue more than anything. It doesn't give a good &quot;Default State&quot; as I would describe it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774365#post774365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Still not seeing why the rulebook needs to explain this.<br /> <br /> More to point though, what we believe shapes what we accept as evidence. For someone who is a scientist there is a &quot;natural laws&quot; explanation for why sparks fly when you strike flint with steel (it has to do with friction and abrasion). An animist will explain that flint does not like steel very much and becomes an angry rock when struck by flint and that is why the sparks fly. The animist is not wrong. Other animists find his explanation adequate.<br /> <br /> The point of the WoD is magic and mystery. Part of the game experience is for the storytellers and players to jointly develop the kind of explanations you seek.</div> </div> </div> </div>The animist is not wrong, just as the scientist is not wrong; they just use different words to convey the same meaning. In your example, animists use much simpler language to make it easier to understand than something you have to learn about (Friction, Abrasion).<br /> <br /> And yes, but world of darkness seems to possess a default state of &quot;It cannot be known&quot; as a cold hard fact, rather than something more flexible. I mean within the current system how would you run someone who's main skill is science? Especially after they've become something other than strictly human (be it a mage, lycanthrope, changeling, etc).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774361#post774361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, we're having a big disconnect here. ReyshyShira, your views about the way science works is completely accurate in real life. But World of Darkness is fiction, and in fiction, if the author says something is unknowable, it's unknowable. The Fae of the World of Darkness complicate these issues further, because the laws they follow are the laws of narrative fiction. Which are malleable.</div> </div> </div> </div>I realize that World of Darkness is fiction, but it supposedly has science in it. So whilst the default state of World of Darkness might be that &quot;These are currently unknown&quot; if you have a Storyteller running a persistent world you can expect the game to <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/ModernStasis\" target=\"_blank\">leave a sort of technological stasis.</a> I'm not saying that this has to be the default state, but at least the setting itself should provide material that at least <b>kind of</b> supports scientific inquiry, instead of relying on absolutes. Might be a minor change in wording, but going from &quot;You can't know this&quot; to &quot;It's incredibly difficult concept to grasp&quot; is at least making it possible.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T17:39:09-08:00","id":774409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774395#post774395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I realize that World of Darkness is fiction, but it supposedly has science in it. </div> </div> </div> </div>It does have science. It also has SCIENCE!!! and whatever the hell you call what happens when H.P. Lovecraft writes science fiction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T17:42:11-08:00","id":774412,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9830_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9830\" data-vbnamecard=\"9830\">ReshyShira</a> I seem to have missed the part where my copies of the rulebooks definitively say that the WoD is unknowable. Mysterious yes. Unknowable no.<br /> <br /> Please do realize that no rulebook will contain all the rules you want. We can't even do that with text books irl. If you want more details, then take matters in hand and houserule it. It's a storyteller and troupes most sacred type of pact.<br /> <br /> But please don't look for definitive answers that we all would have to kowtow to. You'll just be making everyone else's house ruling harder. And some of us aren't going to agree with what you come up with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T18:02:47-08:00","id":774427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774412#post774412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9830_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9830\" data-vbnamecard=\"9830\">ReshyShira</a> I seem to have missed the part where my copies of the rulebooks definitively say that the WoD is unknowable. Mysterious yes. Unknowable no.<br /> <br /> Please do realize that no rulebook will contain all the rules you want. We can't even do that with text books irl. If you want more details, then take matters in hand and houserule it. It's a storyteller and troupes most sacred type of pact.<br /> <br /> But please don't look for definitive answers that we all would have to kowtow to. You'll just be making everyone else's house ruling harder. And some of us aren't going to agree with what you come up with.</div> </div> </div> </div>About the Unknowable thing, I'm mostly referencing the attitudes other players have shown for it. I realize no rulebook will have all the answers (or rules), but what rules it does give should put up a good foundation to base the rest of the game. Furthermore, while I realize that the game is driven by the storyteller, it is nice to have a good &quot;default state&quot; to use as a springboard. The problem is that Cold Iron is a Mechanics issue, and less of a Fluff issue. The mechanics of a game should be reasonably bug free and solid, more so than the fluff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","user":"ReshyShira","date":". 11-25-2015, 09:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T18:27:45-08:00","id":774437,"title":"","content":"I assure you that the mechanics of these games are both reasonably bug free and &quot;solid&quot;. People house rule because the rules are robust enough to allow multiple interpretations. That said there are hard limitations for rulebooks in the form of page counts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T18:32:03-08:00","id":774440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774437#post774437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assure you that the mechanics of these games are both reasonably bug free and &quot;solid&quot;. People house rule because the rules are robust enough to allow multiple interpretations. That said there are hard limitations for rulebooks in the form of page counts.</div> </div> </div> </div>This whole topic is about Cold Iron (Or was supposed to be, before it went massively off-topic). Have you read the rules regarding Cold Iron? Because from what I have read about them, they're about as inconsistent as you can get.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T18:49:06-08:00","id":774450,"title":"","content":"I apologize if I am restating something that has already been said but I read three pages in and then skipped ahead. In Changeling all of their powers, their very reality, is based upon contracts. A leads to B because someone made a contract with A that B would happen. In the case of the True Fae their weakness isn't caused by anything involving science or rational explanations but because there is either a contract that makes them vulnerable, or there isn't a contract that affords them extra protection. It could be that there is no contract with iron so it leaves them vulnerable, but there is a contract with fire that protects them from anything it has wrought. What is needed are the details of the contract.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T19:33:25-08:00","id":774482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774440#post774440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This whole topic is about Cold Iron (Or was supposed to be, before it went massively off-topic). Have you read the rules regarding Cold Iron? Because from what I have read about them, they're about as inconsistent as you can get.</div> </div> </div> </div>My understanding is that Changeling 2nd is in the dev process and probably won't be out until sometime next Fall at the earliest. So no, I haven't. <br /> <br /> I can take a look if you post a link or drop them here, assuming that's okay with the devs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T21:25:56-08:00","id":774530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774450#post774450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I apologize if I am restating something that has already been said but I read three pages in and then skipped ahead. In Changeling all of their powers, their very reality, is based upon contracts. A leads to B because someone made a contract with A that B would happen. In the case of the True Fae their weakness isn't caused by anything involving science or rational explanations but because there is either a contract that makes them vulnerable, or there isn't a contract that affords them extra protection. It could be that there is no contract with iron so it leaves them vulnerable, but there is a contract with fire that protects them from anything it has wrought. What is needed are the details of the contract.</div> </div> </div> </div>I vaguely remember in one of the books (Equinox Road? Not sure) where it mentions one possible source: the Fae did a deal with Iron for protection, but betrayed it, so basically it's the equivalent of a Poisoning the Boon effect.<br /> <br /> *shrug* I like that as a cause. Has its issues, because it implies that Fae can break pledges, but still kind of cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T00:01:42-08:00","id":774574,"title":"","content":"My interpretation:<br /> What qualifies as iron for the purposes of bypassing Faerie defenses is a matter of its conceptual purity, not it's chemical purity. Whatever the origins of the weakness, it comes from a time well before the periodic table. So the weakness isn't to the chemical element iron but to what earlier (possibly prehistoric) cultures thought of as iron. It refers to the raw material as it's pulled from the ground. Iron ore is iron in it's purest form by this way of thinking. The more man alters it or manipulates it, the less conceptually pure it is, and the less effective it is against the Fae. Pig iron, wrought iron, and cast iron qualify because although the iron ore has been melted and worked, it hasn't been changed sufficiently to affect its identity. Steel on the other hand has been transformed through lengthier processes that either require a herculean effort (using ancient methods) or a large-scale industrial process in modern times. The transformation into steel is considerable enough that, conceptually, what is created isn't iron in the sense that was understood at the time of the contract or curse or whatever it may have been. It's not thought of as iron, so much as something that's made from iron. A completely pure sample of the chemical element Fe wouldn't work as a bane, since it doesn't occur that way in nature and would have to be produced by complex scientific procedures. Plus, it's nothing like the conception of iron that existed at the time the bane came into existence.<br /> <br /> Determining what works is less a matter of science and more a matter of legality. When a Judge has to make a ruling on how to interpret the language of a contract, they take into account what the terms meant when the contract was written up to determine the intent. In this case the Judge is the Wyrd, and it has determined that the iron in question is the ancient material and not the chemical element that people named after it much, much later. You could try to get the Wyrd to reconsider its ruling, but the Gentry aren't interested in expanding their bane and they have better lawyers than you, metaphorically.<br /> <br /> The books do muddy the waters by saying contradictory things about what constitutes &quot;pure&quot; iron, and by either not understanding how wrought and cast iron are made or just being written in a confusing way.<br /> <br /> Side note:<br /> I also felt that the requirements for making hand-forged iron presented in RoS were both vague and excessively difficult. Personally, I allow any iron made with ancient methods (not using any modern processes or machinery), to count in my games. This makes it possible for regular people to acquire hand-forged iron, but means that characters either have to go on a search for a smith, find an antique that suits their needs, or learn to craft the items themselves. This is just a personal preference/house rule, obviously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T11:18:22-08:00","id":774923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774450#post774450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I apologize if I am restating something that has already been said but I read three pages in and then skipped ahead. In Changeling all of their powers, their very reality, is based upon contracts. A leads to B because someone made a contract with A that B would happen. In the case of the True Fae their weakness isn't caused by anything involving science or rational explanations but because there is either a contract that makes them vulnerable, or there isn't a contract that affords them extra protection. It could be that there is no contract with iron so it leaves them vulnerable, but there is a contract with fire that protects them from anything it has wrought. What is needed are the details of the contract.</div> </div> </div> </div>The second you know how contract law works, it can be made into a science. What are the limitations of Fae magic? What has it been shown to be capable of doing? What Fuels it? etc. You could in essence make a field of science that deals with Fae magic. I think you don't understand what science is too well. <a href=\"http://www.cdn.sciencebuddies.org/Files/5084/7/2013-updated_scientific-method-steps_v6_noheader.png\" target=\"_blank\">Here's how science works</a><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scientific_method\" target=\"_blank\">.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774482#post774482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My understanding is that Changeling 2nd is in the dev process and probably won't be out until sometime next Fall at the earliest. So no, I haven't.<br /> <br /> I can take a look if you post a link or drop them here, assuming that's okay with the devs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am referencing 1e's Cold Iron Definition (or lack thereof). If you read the first two posts you'd know what we were talking about.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774574#post774574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My interpretation:<br /> What qualifies as iron for the purposes of bypassing Faerie defenses is a matter of its conceptual purity, not it's chemical purity. Whatever the origins of the weakness, it comes from a time well before the periodic table. So the weakness isn't to the chemical element iron but to what earlier (possibly prehistoric) cultures thought of as iron. It refers to the raw material as it's pulled from the ground. Iron ore is iron in it's purest form by this way of thinking. The more man alters it or manipulates it, the less conceptually pure it is, and the less effective it is against the Fae. Pig iron, wrought iron, and cast iron qualify because although the iron ore has been melted and worked, it hasn't been changed sufficiently to affect its identity. Steel on the other hand has been transformed through lengthier processes that either require a herculean effort (using ancient methods) or a large-scale industrial process in modern times. The transformation into steel is considerable enough that, conceptually, what is created isn't iron in the sense that was understood at the time of the contract or curse or whatever it may have been. It's not thought of as iron, so much as something that's made from iron. A completely pure sample of the chemical element Fe wouldn't work as a bane, since it doesn't occur that way in nature and would have to be produced by complex scientific procedures. Plus, it's nothing like the conception of iron that existed at the time the bane came into existence.<br /> <br /> Determining what works is less a matter of science and more a matter of legality. When a Judge has to make a ruling on how to interpret the language of a contract, they take into account what the terms meant when the contract was written up to determine the intent. In this case the Judge is the Wyrd, and it has determined that the iron in question is the ancient material and not the chemical element that people named after it much, much later. You could try to get the Wyrd to reconsider its ruling, but the Gentry aren't interested in expanding their bane and they have better lawyers than you, metaphorically.<br /> <br /> The books do muddy the waters by saying contradictory things about what constitutes &quot;pure&quot; iron, and by either not understanding how wrought and cast iron are made or just being written in a confusing way.<br /> <br /> Side note:<br /> I also felt that the requirements for making hand-forged iron presented in RoS were both vague and excessively difficult. Personally, I allow any iron made with ancient methods (not using any modern processes or machinery), to count in my games. This makes it possible for regular people to acquire hand-forged iron, but means that characters either have to go on a search for a smith, find an antique that suits their needs, or learn to craft the items themselves. This is just a personal preference/house rule, obviously.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pig Iron doesn't have that conceptual purify thing going.<br /> &quot;Pig Iron: Pig iron is raw iron immediately after it has been smelted in a blast furnace. Pig iron\u2019s high carbon content makes it far too brittle for use in construction, but pig iron can be found in limited applications such as weights and anchors. Because it has been heated, pig iron does not inflict aggravated damage against the Others.&quot;<br /> <br /> This means that Cast Iron and Wrought Iron probably don't have those properties either, which is weird because they constantly use &quot;you pick a piece of a fence off and use it as a weapon and it doesn't work because steel.&quot; Perhaps it's a case of an unreliable narrator, as it also describes steel as being a &quot;cheap imitation&quot; despite it not and not.<br /> <br /> The problem is of course that the game <b>constantly</b> muddles the issue between &quot;conceptual purity&quot; and &quot;literal purity&quot; which is the main problem I am talking about.<br /> <br /> And actually, being able to use unprocessed unrefined materials to bane the Fae would actually be a benefit, because it's even cheaper. You can buy Iron Ore Pellets by the ton. So a cheap nearly ubiquitous source of &quot;hand-wrought cold iron&quot; in the form of several tonnes of Iron Ore could easily be weaponized. Buying a single high-carbon steel sword is easily a thousand dollars, buying several tons of material is probably in the similar price range.<br /> <br /> I am all for using powered iron ore dust on everything, but I doubt that's what the designers intended to be the bane of the Fae being the equivalent of anti-Fairy Dust. It'd be amusing though.<br /> <br /> <br /> Simply speaking, it seems (to me) that &quot;Cold Iron&quot; in the games were not well thought out. Many examples in folk lore deal more with processed irons, and not unrefined materials. So I don't get why &quot;Steel&quot; can't be used against Fae, despite it being expensive; but an incredibly cheap unrefined material can. Can you imagine killing a True Fae with a sling shot or by throwing a bag of dust on them? Seems silly and anti-climatic to me. Albeit this is the Fae, so they are silly by nature.<br /> <br /> <br /> Again, the problem with defining those is that the processes have always evolved over time. When something stops being a &quot;tool&quot; and starts being a &quot;machine&quot; isn't defined.<br /> <br /> Also let's see what Cold Iron is in folk lore (Taken from Wikipedia).<br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Francis_Grose\" target=\"_blank\">Francis Grose's</a> <i>1811 Dictionary of the Vulgar Tongue</i> defines cold iron as &quot;A sword, or any other weapon for cutting or stabbing.&quot;<br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rudyard_Kipling\" target=\"_blank\">Rudyard Kipling</a>'s poem &quot;<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cold_Iron_%28poem%29\" target=\"_blank\">Cold Iron</a>&quot;, found in his 1910 collection of stories <i><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rewards_and_Fairies\" target=\"_blank\">Rewards and Fairies</a></i>, used the term poetically to mean &quot;weapon&quot;.<br /> <br /> I believe Changeling's definition makes no sense from either a &quot;balance&quot; or a mythological perspective. Unrefined Iron Ore is cheap and plentiful, the stories clearly intended manufactured weapons made of iron and are modern enough that &quot;modern techniques&quot; shouldn't invalidate these stories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","user":"ReshyShira","date":". 11-26-2015, 02:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T11:35:40-08:00","id":774934,"title":"","content":"It's been simplified.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T12:54:13-08:00","id":774974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774934#post774934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's been simplified.</div> </div> </div> </div>QFT.<br /> <br /> In 1e, the Cold Iron issue was somewhat inconsistently defined and a cause of much argument. In 2e, it will be much clearer and more consistent. I don't know what else to tell you ReshyShira. For now, use what ever definition works for you in your games, and when 2e comes out, hopefully the new definition will suit your needs. If it doesn't, no one will come take your books away if you continue to use the definition you prefer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T13:08:31-08:00","id":774988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774974#post774974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">QFT.<br /> <br /> In 1e, the Cold Iron issue was somewhat inconsistently defined and a cause of much argument. In 2e, it will be much clearer and more consistent. I don't know what else to tell you ReshyShira. For now, use what ever definition works for you in your games, and when 2e comes out, hopefully the new definition will suit your needs. If it doesn't, no one will come take your books away if you continue to use the definition you prefer.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's all I'm asking for, thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T13:52:44-08:00","id":775008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774923#post774923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pig Iron doesn't have that conceptual purify thing going.<br /> &quot;Pig Iron: Pig iron is raw iron immediately after it has been smelted in a blast furnace. Pig iron\u2019s high carbon content makes it far too brittle for use in construction, but pig iron can be found in limited applications such as weights and anchors. Because it has been heated, pig iron does not inflict aggravated damage against the Others.&quot;<br /> <br /> This means that Cast Iron and Wrought Iron probably don't have those properties either, which is weird because they constantly use &quot;you pick a piece of a fence off and use it as a weapon and it doesn't work because steel.&quot; Perhaps it's a case of an unreliable narrator, as it also describes steel as being a &quot;cheap imitation&quot; despite it not and not.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> I'm talking about it qualifying for negating Fae magic defenses, not doing agg. It's identity has been diluted enough to not do agg, but is still intact enough to cut through Fae magic. The only thing that counts for doing agg by the RAW is Iron that hasn't been smelted, which is pretty much impossible to use as a weapon unless you use the (incredibly vague) rules presented in RoS for hand-forging meteoric ore without heat via weird Fae tricks.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774923#post774923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is of course that the game <b>constantly</b> muddles the issue between &quot;conceptual purity&quot; and &quot;literal purity&quot; which is the main problem I am talking about.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I totally agree. You can use the context clues provided, though, (primarily what they say counts and what doesn't) to infer that what they meant had a lot more to do with conceptual purity than chemical composition. But the writing is definitely super unclear.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774923#post774923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And actually, being able to use unprocessed unrefined materials to bane the Fae would actually be a benefit, because it's even cheaper. You can buy Iron Ore Pellets by the ton. So a cheap nearly ubiquitous source of &quot;hand-wrought cold iron&quot; in the form of several tonnes of Iron Ore could easily be weaponized. Buying a single high-carbon steel sword is easily a thousand dollars, buying several tons of material is probably in the similar price range.<br /> <br /> I am all for using powered iron ore dust on everything, but I doubt that's what the designers intended to be the bane of the Fae being the equivalent of anti-Fairy Dust. It'd be amusing though.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I like that, actually. It'd be like salt in Supernatural. Would be pretty hard to use it to do damage, but it could serve as a barrier. It's less readily available than salt in everyday life. and definitely nowhere near as ubiquitous as steel.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774923#post774923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Simply speaking, it seems (to me) that &quot;Cold Iron&quot; in the games were not well thought out. Many examples in folk lore deal more with processed irons, and not unrefined materials. So I don't get why &quot;Steel&quot; can't be used against Fae, despite it being expensive; but an incredibly cheap unrefined material can. Can you imagine killing a True Fae with a sling shot or by throwing a bag of dust on them? Seems silly and anti-climatic to me. Albeit this is the Fae, so they are silly by nature.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> That's the thing; iron ore is an extremely ineffective weapon. You'll shoot a Gentry with one chunk of iron ore from your slingshot, and, if you even hit, do an agg or two. Then the Fae crams the slingshot down your throat. You could somehow rig up a trap to drop a literal ton of iron on the Other, but the kind of planning and forethought that such a trap would require, and the need to trick the Fae into standing in just the right place, seems like a perfectly satisfying way to kill one of the Gentry to me.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774923#post774923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, the problem with defining those is that the processes have always evolved over time. When something stops being a &quot;tool&quot; and starts being a &quot;machine&quot; isn't defined.<br /> <br /> Also let's see what Cold Iron is in folk lore (Taken from Wikipedia).<br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Francis_Grose\" target=\"_blank\">Francis Grose's</a> <i>1811 Dictionary of the Vulgar Tongue</i> defines cold iron as &quot;A sword, or any other weapon for cutting or stabbing.&quot;<br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rudyard_Kipling\" target=\"_blank\">Rudyard Kipling</a>'s poem &quot;<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cold_Iron_%28poem%29\" target=\"_blank\">Cold Iron</a>&quot;, found in his 1910 collection of stories <i><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rewards_and_Fairies\" target=\"_blank\">Rewards and Fairies</a></i>, used the term poetically to mean &quot;weapon&quot;.<br /> <br /> I believe Changeling's definition makes no sense from either a &quot;balance&quot; or a mythological perspective. Unrefined Iron Ore is cheap and plentiful, the stories clearly intended manufactured weapons made of iron and are modern enough that &quot;modern techniques&quot; shouldn't invalidate these stories.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm aware of how the term was used, yes. That's pretty clearly not what they intended in the core book. They probably thought the Fae having a weakness to swords was just too easy. Then again, it would work just fine in my chronicles, since (combat-quality) swords are as rare as they are in the real world and none of my players or NPCs just go walking around with them. And if you can manage to take down one of the Gentry with a kitchen knife, well, I think you deserve to. Hell, it hasn't really come up in my current game, so I might consider allowing it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T15:23:44-08:00","id":775061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=774923#post774923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The second you know how contract law works, it can be made into a science. What are the limitations of Fae magic? What has it been shown to be capable of doing? What Fuels it? etc. You could in essence make a field of science that deals with Fae magic. I think you don't understand what science is too well. <a href=\"http://www.cdn.sciencebuddies.org/Files/5084/7/2013-updated_scientific-method-steps_v6_noheader.png\" target=\"_blank\">Here's how science works</a><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scientific_method\" target=\"_blank\">.</a><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I'm unclear. So you're insisting that the reason the Fae - near-purely chaotic beings from a land of dreams and nightmares - are bothered by iron should be consistent with the physical laws which humanity - consistently portrayed as an immensely ignorant species in the World of Darkness - has come up with, mostly over the course of the last few hundred years, and despite the books portraying the Fae as Lovecraftian entities governed by laws that make basically zero sense from our perspective, and which they more than likely come up with themselves and change on a whim, you think the books should set down something like &quot;The Fae take aggravated damage from iron because its magnetic properties interfere with the electromagnetic energies derived from the human brain* while in a particular state of REM sleep, and this property is only shown when it's in this certain configuration because that maximises its magnetic conductivity and thus disruptive abilities&quot;?<br /> <br /> It's your game, and you can run it how you like. Me? I like more Lovecraft in my World of Darkness - the idea that the universe doesn't make sense, and that we've cobbled together these physical laws that are woefully inadequate at best, and laughable most often in a desperate attempt to pretend it's remotely controllable. With the different definitions of cold iron all simultanously being true, because there is no pattern to the Fae.<br /> <br /> *Yes, I know the brain doesn't give off electromagnetic energies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T17:55:02-08:00","id":775122,"title":"","content":"I dare say the whole intent of unwrought iron was to include a bane that characters have to obtain specifically, not just find lying around the average kitchen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T18:12:00-08:00","id":775128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=775061#post775061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, I'm unclear. So you're insisting that the reason the Fae - near-purely chaotic beings from a land of dreams and nightmares - are bothered by iron should be consistent with the physical laws which humanity - consistently portrayed as an immensely ignorant species in the World of Darkness - has come up with</div> </div> </div> </div>That isn't what we're saying at all. We're saying that them being bothered by iron IS consistent with the physical laws of reality, regardless of how little humanity truly knows in the World of Darkness. Humans are ridiculously ignorant, yes (Mages are slightly less ignorant), that is our point. Just because you don't know How or Why something happens, doesn't mean there isn't one. There is always one, or it wouldn't of happened, because something can only happen if something makes it happen. Science isn't the laws we Think exist, science is the process of discovery and rules behind reality. Gentry are harmed by Cold Iron. That's true. You can repeat it, over and over. Humanity might not understand why certain types of iron work, and why others do. You can find &quot;okay steel doesn't work, so it isn't to do with the purity of iron&quot; that's science in action. Even if the How and Why literally are &quot;The Gentry broke an oath to the concept of Iron itself&quot;, that can be the Scientific Reason for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T18:42:55-08:00","id":775149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=775008#post775008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm talking about it qualifying for negating Fae magic defenses, not doing agg. It's identity has been diluted enough to not do agg, but is still intact enough to cut through Fae magic. The only thing that counts for doing agg by the RAW is Iron that hasn't been smelted, which is pretty much impossible to use as a weapon unless you use the (incredibly vague) rules presented in RoS for hand-forging meteoric ore without heat via weird Fae tricks.[/SIZE][/FONT][/COLOR]<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I totally agree. You can use the context clues provided, though, (primarily what they say counts and what doesn't) to infer that what they meant had a lot more to do with conceptual purity than chemical composition. But the writing is definitely super unclear.<br /> <br /> [COLOR=#252C2F][FONT=Helvetica][SIZE=13px]<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I like that, actually. It'd be like salt in Supernatural. Would be pretty hard to use it to do damage, but it could serve as a barrier. It's less readily available than salt in everyday life. and definitely nowhere near as ubiquitous as steel.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> That's the thing; iron ore is an extremely ineffective weapon. You'll shoot a Gentry with one chunk of iron ore from your slingshot, and, if you even hit, do an agg or two. Then the Fae crams the slingshot down your throat. You could somehow rig up a trap to drop a literal ton of iron on the Other, but the kind of planning and forethought that such a trap would require, and the need to trick the Fae into standing in just the right place, seems like a perfectly satisfying way to kill one of the Gentry to me.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> [COLOR=#252C2F][FONT=Helvetica][SIZE=13px]<br /> <br /> I'm aware of how the term was used, yes. That's pretty clearly not what they intended in the core book. They probably thought the Fae having a weakness to swords was just too easy. Then again, it would work just fine in my chronicles, since (combat-quality) swords are as rare as they are in the real world and none of my players or NPCs just go walking around with them. And if you can manage to take down one of the Gentry with a kitchen knife, well, I think you deserve to. Hell, it hasn't really come up in my current game, so I might consider allowing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is that if that is still &quot;Cold Iron&quot; after it's been heated, then what makes a low-carbon steel inferior to a Cast Iron/Wrought Iron weapon.<br /> <br /> Yes, I realize it's not be an effective &quot;weapon&quot; but against the Gentry it doesn't need to be a &quot;Literal Weapon&quot; when it's intended to be used as a &quot;Conceptual Weapon.&quot; Get what I mean? Just because it's not good for killing the thud down the block doesn't make it less effective against the Gentry. Some of the Gentry cannot handle the cries of a young lass, yet obviously the cries of a young lass aren't a brilliant defensive weapon in the physical.<br /> <br /> As for the topic of delivery method, I was thinking more along the lines of a <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eObepuHvYAw\" target=\"_blank\">Railgun</a> or <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7LjnhhtHojM\" target=\"_blank\">Coilgun</a>, something portable that can launch a magnetic sphere of unrefined iron at high velocities. Only issue would be getting it portable, though of course you could just mount it on a vehicle and call it good.<br /> <br /> <br /> I would have to wonder though, why do you think them having a weakness to swords is too easy? In a world where firearms are everywhere and much more effective than swords (Not to mention much easier to conceal), why shouldn't it be effective? You still have to get up close and personal to the Gentry, not blow them apart from 3 miles away with an antimaterial round (Not that you couldn't do that, since they're not invulnerable just harder to kill without it). As for the kitchen knife thing, most kitchen knives are made of <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xGTQLB1VQrA\" target=\"_blank\">Stainless Steel, which is full of chromium (sometimes more than the actual iron) so it's brittle and breaks easily</a> (I have a large interest in <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=t-EodSILCi0\" target=\"_blank\">medieval weaponry</a>). However, if you happen to have a Cast Iron Pot or a Wrought Iron Fireplace Poker, that's effectively the same problem though isn't it? Heck, Pig Iron, Wrought Iron, and Cast Iron are often cheaper than high-quality steels. Anyway, we both more or less agree in the end, but it doesn't seem like the core rule book seems to agree. The definition in the book basically has not really occured in history. Most weapons (if not all) were forged with some amount of heat, for instance.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=775061#post775061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, I'm unclear. So you're insisting that the reason the Fae - near-purely chaotic beings from a land of dreams and nightmares - are bothered by iron should be consistent with the physical laws which humanity - consistently portrayed as an immensely ignorant species in the World of Darkness - has come up with, mostly over the course of the last few hundred years, and despite the books portraying the Fae as Lovecraftian entities governed by laws that make basically zero sense from our perspective, and which they more than likely come up with themselves and change on a whim, you think the books should set down something like &quot;The Fae take aggravated damage from iron because its magnetic properties interfere with the electromagnetic energies derived from the human brain* while in a particular state of REM sleep, and this property is only shown when it's in this certain configuration because that maximises its magnetic conductivity and thus disruptive abilities&quot;?<br /> <br /> It's your game, and you can run it how you like. Me? I like more Lovecraft in my World of Darkness - the idea that the universe doesn't make sense, and that we've cobbled together these physical laws that are woefully inadequate at best, and laughable most often in a desperate attempt to pretend it's remotely controllable. With the different definitions of cold iron all simultanously being true, because there is no pattern to the Fae.<br /> <br /> *Yes, I know the brain doesn't give off electromagnetic energies.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem I have with it is that it's so specific that I doubt that a single &quot;Hand-Wrought Cold Iron&quot; weapon has ever really been made. It's so oddly specific that it's almost a non-vulnerability. It's like taking damage from Unobtanium. No one's going to have that. And if no one has that, then why to the True Fae seem to worry about older humans resisting being dragged into the hedge if the vast majority of them do not possess any kind of defense? It's not consistent with the rest of the fluff.<br /> <br /> The books make it out to be that the True Fae hesitate to kidnap an adult because they're able to &quot;defend themselves better&quot; however if you even looked at the actors then you'd know this is pretty much objectively wrong. They could walk down the street and probably make a big scene and still be perfectly fine. The only mitigating factor I could think of is that due to how much Iron we use in our society, things that could wield a weapon against them are inherently dangerous to them. However, it then goes on to pile on a dozen restrictions on what &quot;effective iron&quot; is to the point where it's basically a non-factor. Again, it's a consistency issue. Why would the Gentry fear abducting adult humans when they're probably able to drag them away without much (if any) resistance.<br /> <br /> <br /> Okay, you're free to run the game how you want to. No one's going to hold you down and make you follow the rules. Heck you could also just go play Trail of Cthulhu, seems like it'd fit what you conceptually want better. If you want to have your players blindly fumble through a game and be unable to learn anything because &quot;lol universe soooo random&quot; that's fine, I have the right not to play with you. If you're saying that humans would be incapable of understanding or even knowing about such beings in any remotely realistic capacity, then I reserve the right to call you out for being wrong.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=775122#post775122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dare say the whole intent of unwrought iron was to include a bane that characters have to obtain specifically, not just find lying around the average kitchen.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about your fireplace poker? Heck, if you need one just order them online.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T21:55:30-08:00","id":775247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=775149#post775149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The thing is that if that is still &quot;Cold Iron&quot; after it's been heated, then what makes a low-carbon steel inferior to a Cast Iron/Wrought Iron weapon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Imagine that an archeo-metallurgist is classifying the item. If they'd call it iron, it counts for the bane. If they'd say it's steel, it doesn't.<br /> <br /> Steel is different enough from the iron that was known to the world when the bane was born, that it doesn't qualify. Plus, it has a different name and names are powerful to the Fae. Hell, it's possible that some tricky Gentry got people to invent the word steel specifically to weaken the bane because people were improving iron too much.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;What's that you've got there blacksmith?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I found a way to make iron much stronger than before, but it was very brittle. Now I've discovered a method for making the iron not just strong, but tough as well. And it will return to it's original shape if bent.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;That's amazing! What a wondrous thing you have made. This is no mere iron! Surely, it is something new. You must give it a new name, that men might fear and covet it.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;You're right. Something that brings to mind strength and durability...&quot;<br /> <br /> *chuckles*</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=775149#post775149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, I realize it's not be an effective &quot;weapon&quot; but against the Gentry it doesn't need to be a &quot;Literal Weapon&quot; when it's intended to be used as a &quot;Conceptual Weapon.&quot; Get what I mean? Just because it's not good for killing the thud down the block doesn't make it less effective against the Gentry. Some of the Gentry cannot handle the cries of a young lass, yet obviously the cries of a young lass aren't a brilliant defensive weapon in the physical.</div> </div> </div> </div>Something that's an effective conceptual weapon <i>and</i> an effective literal weapon is best for fighting the Gentry. You might be able to drive a True Fae off with a chunk of iron ore, or maybe even hurt it a little if you manage to touch it, but you're better off using an iron sword if you want to kill it. An iron horse shoe over your door will piss it off and make it find another way in, but iron buckshot will ruin its day.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=775149#post775149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the topic of delivery method, I was thinking more along the lines of a <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eObepuHvYAw\" target=\"_blank\">Railgun</a> or <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7LjnhhtHojM\" target=\"_blank\">Coilgun</a>, something portable that can launch a magnetic sphere of unrefined iron at high velocities. Only issue would be getting it portable, though of course you could just mount it on a vehicle and call it good.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have yet to have a PC who was an engineer with a lot of free time and disposable income in my games. If I had a player go through the trouble to design and create a railgun or coilgun, though, I think that'd be a pretty awesome way to take out a Gentry. They'd probably only get one shot, though. As soon as the True Fae realizes what the hell that thing is, it's scrap.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=775149#post775149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would have to wonder though, why do you think them having a weakness to swords is too easy? In a world where firearms are everywhere and much more effective than swords (Not to mention much easier to conceal), why shouldn't it be effective? You still have to get up close and personal to the Gentry, not blow them apart from 3 miles away with an antimaterial round (Not that you couldn't do that, since they're not invulnerable just harder to kill without it). As for the kitchen knife thing, most kitchen knives are made of <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xGTQLB1VQrA\" target=\"_blank\">Stainless Steel, which is full of chromium (sometimes more than the actual iron) so it's brittle and breaks easily</a> (I have a large interest in <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=t-EodSILCi0\" target=\"_blank\">medieval weaponry</a>). However, if you happen to have a Cast Iron Pot or a Wrought Iron Fireplace Poker, that's effectively the same problem though isn't it? Heck, Pig Iron, Wrought Iron, and Cast Iron are often cheaper than high-quality steels. Anyway, we both more or less agree in the end, but it doesn't seem like the core rule book seems to agree. The definition in the book basically has not really occured in history. Most weapons (if not all) were forged with some amount of heat, for instance.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't say that <i>I</i> think that it's too easy, I was just taking a guess at why the writers made the differentiation. Which is why I wrote &quot;they probably thought.&quot; Like I said, in my chronicles it would probably be fine, and since the question of what counts as iron hasn't come up in my current game, I might just house rule that steel works just fine.<br /> <br /> As for knives, plenty of folks who like to cook have carbon steel knives, and carbon steel knives are fairly inexpensive and incredibly easy to get your hands on.<br /> <br /> Those fence posts and fireplace pokers are probably actually mild steel that has been given a faux-iron finish, unless they're antiques (well, at least 40+ years old) since commercial wrought iron production was pretty much dead by the mid-70s.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5910,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","user":"CSSchulz","date":". 11-27-2015, 02:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T00:08:01-08:00","id":775300,"title":"","content":"For mine games, I just use Hand Wrought Iron - if Smith was needed to make it by his own hands, it's &quot;Cold&quot; enough. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As to general Cold Iron idea in game:<br /> <br /> <i>True Fae are living stories. And <b>their stories</b> is they are affected by &quot;Cold Iron&quot;, not steel.</i> It's simple as that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=775008#post775008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm aware of how the term was used, yes. That's pretty clearly not what they intended in the core book. They probably thought the Fae having a weakness to swords was just too easy. Then again, it would work just fine in my chronicles, since (combat-quality) swords are as rare as they are in the real world and none of my players or NPCs just go walking around with them. And if you can manage to take down one of the Gentry with a kitchen knife, well, I think you deserve to. Hell, it hasn't really come up in my current game, so I might consider allowing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>But do not whole firerams industry and modern pistols, rifles and all are made from steel? With those intepretations any modern weapon would kill True Fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T00:30:00-08:00","id":775309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=775300#post775300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But do not whole firerams industry and modern pistols, rifles and all are made from steel? With those intepretations any modern weapon would kill True Fae.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bullets are usually made from lead. Some are jacketed with steel, but that probably wouldn't be enough to count for bane purposes. Even if it was enough to count, steel jacketed bullets are usually plated with another metal (like copper) to avoid corrosion, which means the steel would be covered up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T03:00:15-08:00","id":775349,"title":"","content":"Better question is this - <b>Is Cold Iron the one made by blacksmithing?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T06:27:43-08:00","id":775427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=775349#post775349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Better question is this - <b>Is Cold Iron the one made by blacksmithing?</b></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not by the rules as written, but that's certainly a reasonable house rule. Bear in mind that it would be fairly easy to make iron bullets in a forge via blacksmithing, either way. Ammunition would actually be one of the easiest weapons to make to use against the True Fae. Making a few dozen iron bullets would be a piece of cake compared to making a sword, for instance. You just couldn't buy them right off the shelf at Cabelas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T13:52:34-08:00","id":775615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=775247#post775247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Imagine that an archeo-metallurgist is classifying the item. If they'd call it iron, it counts for the bane. If they'd say it's steel, it doesn't.<br /> <br /> Steel is different enough from the iron that was known to the world when the bane was born, that it doesn't qualify. Plus, it has a different name and names are powerful to the Fae. Hell, it's possible that some tricky Gentry got people to invent the word steel specifically to weaken the bane because people were improving iron too much.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;What's that you've got there blacksmith?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I found a way to make iron much stronger than before, but it was very brittle. Now I've discovered a method for making the iron not just strong, but tough as well. And it will return to it's original shape if bent.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;That's amazing! What a wondrous thing you have made. This is no mere iron! Surely, it is something new. You must give it a new name, that men might fear and covet it.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;You're right. Something that brings to mind strength and durability...&quot;<br /> <br /> *chuckles*</i><br /> <br /> Something that's an effective conceptual weapon <i>and</i> an effective literal weapon is best for fighting the Gentry. You might be able to drive a True Fae off with a chunk of iron ore, or maybe even hurt it a little if you manage to touch it, but you're better off using an iron sword if you want to kill it. An iron horse shoe over your door will piss it off and make it find another way in, but iron buckshot will ruin its day.<br /> <br /> I have yet to have a PC who was an engineer with a lot of free time and disposable income in my games. If I had a player go through the trouble to design and create a railgun or coilgun, though, I think that'd be a pretty awesome way to take out a Gentry. They'd probably only get one shot, though. As soon as the True Fae realizes what the hell that thing is, it's scrap.<br /> <br /> I didn't say that <i>I</i> think that it's too easy, I was just taking a guess at why the writers made the differentiation. Which is why I wrote &quot;they probably thought.&quot; Like I said, in my chronicles it would probably be fine, and since the question of what counts as iron hasn't come up in my current game, I might just house rule that steel works just fine.<br /> <br /> As for knives, plenty of folks who like to cook have carbon steel knives, and carbon steel knives are fairly inexpensive and incredibly easy to get your hands on.<br /> <br /> Those fence posts and fireplace pokers are probably actually mild steel that has been given a faux-iron finish, unless they're antiques (well, at least 40+ years old) since commercial wrought iron production was pretty much dead by the mid-70s.</div> </div> </div> </div>So if you were to formulate a new type of iron alloy and called it &quot;Cold Iron&quot; would it then work? Names matter of course, so so long as it's new it can be called whatever you want it to be.<br /> <br /> Also I realize that both *would* be better, however the books make it very difficult to achieve such an item unless you're very intentionally trying to make something to those exact specifications. That's kind of the issue I have with the current definition, it's so oddly specific that I doubt anyone would know even how to make one. By modern techniques the only way I could see it working is by getting bacteria to &quot;eat&quot; the impurities of the ore and leave the iron in tact, then use a &quot;hammer&quot; to smash it into a roughly functional shape. <br /> <br /> On the topic of the <a href=\"http://media.midwayusa.com/productimages/880x660/Primary/226/979634.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Iron Buckshot</a>, it'd be probably the easiest delivery method, because you could just use <a href=\"http://geo.msu.edu/extra/geogmich/images/iron_ore_pellets.JPG\" target=\"_blank\">unrefined iron ore pellets</a> that have been shaved down small enough. So in essence you have a shotgun that can deal aggravated damage to Fae. Shotguns can be loaded with nearly anything, so putting in round pellets would maintain the shotgun-like performance. Oh and don't forget to <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=M3Hs4do69ms\" target=\"_blank\">buy shotgun Speed loaders</a>. I will say though that I doubt the intent of the rules was to make melee weapons even more useless than they were (another issue with the current rules).<br /> <br /> When it comes down to it, I prefer investigative intellectual types. It's just the kind of character I like to do most. And ideally, you'd only need <b>one shot</b>.<br /> <br /> And yes high-carbon steel is relatively inexpensive, but most of the ones you have around are likely not those. If the material was highly expensive it'd simply not be used. However, that doesn't mean that it's widely used in the house-hold. I mean you can find someone that has knives like those lying around, but majority of people will likely have Stainless Steel. Plus the Gentry are smart, if someone had steel knives and not the flimsy stainless ones they'd look for easier prey.<br /> <br /> Honestly, the only reason why people don't use Wrought Iron is that it's an objectively worse material compared to iron that has been tempered into &quot;steel.&quot; Again, this is another reason why firearms would be better than weaponry against the True Fae, it's cheap and effective to make aggravated damage bullets, but considerably more difficult to do so with actual functional swords. I believe that is an issue to be addressed;. Now you might say it's impossible to get Wrought Iron, and certainly it's much less common now but certain things still use them. <a href=\"http://www.woodlanddirect.com/Pilgrim-30-Vintage-Iron-Single-Fireplace-Tools-Poker?gdftrk=gdfV23673_a_7c1677_a_7c8224_a_7c1142054&amp;gclid=Cj0KEQiAm-CyBRDx65nBhcmVtbIBEiQA7zm8ldUbypfCnjxtA22o6qgEfYPtzwxwQwsJcZXej2kAjV4aApNy8P8HAQ\" target=\"_blank\">Here's</a> something I found in five minutes. Though of course this is real-world stuff I am talking about. If the Gentry were a real threat I'd expect to see many more &quot;Antique Wrought Iron Swordsmiths&quot; putting out advertisements with tongue-and-cheek references to warding off faeries.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=775300#post775300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For mine games, I just use Hand Wrought Iron - if Smith was needed to make it by his own hands, it's &quot;Cold&quot; enough. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As to general Cold Iron idea in game:<br /> <br /> <i>True Fae are living stories. And <b>their stories</b> is they are affected by &quot;Cold Iron&quot;, not steel.</i> It's simple as that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But do not whole firerams industry and modern pistols, rifles and all are made from steel? With those intepretations any modern weapon would kill True Fae.</div> </div> </div> </div>But when is iron no longer iron but steel?<br /> <br /> Also in the mythology as I understand it yes our world is supposed to be <b>toxic</b> to them, hence the aversion to things made of iron. Changeling just modifies this because otherwise why be scared of faeries when everything is made of iron.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T14:59:49-08:00","id":775640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=775615#post775615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So if you were to formulate a new type of iron alloy and called it &amp;quot;Cold Iron&amp;quot; would it then work? Names matter of course, so so long as it's new it can be called whatever you want it to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would have to be close enough to iron that ancient people would still identify it as iron. It needs to fit the meaning that the term had when the bane was conceived. This is why you can't brain a gentry with a modern clothes iron; it's called an iron, but it's clearly not what the bane refers to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=775615#post775615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also I realize that both *would* be better, however the books make it very difficult to achieve such an item unless you're very intentionally trying to make something to those exact specifications. That's kind of the issue I have with the current definition, it's so oddly specific that I doubt anyone would know even how to make one. By modern techniques the only way I could see it working is by getting bacteria to &amp;quot;eat&amp;quot; the impurities of the ore and leave the iron in tact, then use a &amp;quot;hammer&amp;quot; to smash it into a roughly functional shape.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I said, I agree that the requirements for iron to qualify to do agg are excessively restrictive. Again, I house rule it so that it just needs to be forged without machines or modern techniques.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=775615#post775615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the topic of the <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://media.midwayusa.com/productimages/880x660/Primary/226/979634.jpg&amp;quot;]Iron</a> Buckshot[/URL], it'd be probably the easiest delivery method, because you could just use <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://geo.msu.edu/extra/geogmich/images/iron_ore_pellets.JPG&amp;quot;]unrefined</a> iron ore pellets[/URL] that have been shaved down small enough. So in essence you have a shotgun that can deal aggravated damage to Fae. Shotguns can be loaded with nearly anything, so putting in round pellets would maintain the shotgun-like performance. Oh and don't forget to <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=M3Hs4do69ms&amp;quot;]buy</a> shotgun Speed loaders[/URL]. I will say though that I doubt the intent of the rules was to make melee weapons even more useless than they were (another issue with the current rules).</div> </div> </div> </div>Iron buckshot has been the most common iron weapon I've seen used in games, both in CtL and CtD.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=775615#post775615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When it comes down to it, I prefer investigative intellectual types. It's just the kind of character I like to do most. And ideally, you'd only need <b>one shot</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do too, they've just tended towards Academics and occultists in my games. As opposed to Macgyvers and Batmans (Batmen?).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=775615#post775615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yes high-carbon steel is relatively inexpensive, but most of the ones you have around are likely not those. If the material was highly expensive it'd simply not be used. However, that doesn't mean that it's widely used in the house-hold. I mean you can find someone that has knives like those lying around, but majority of people will likely have Stainless Steel. Plus the Gentry are smart, if someone had steel knives and not the flimsy stainless ones they'd look for easier prey.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just meant they'd be easier to acquire than swords or genuine wrought iron. Personally, I know more people who own carbon steel knives than I do who have legit wrought iron fireplace pokers. But that's anecdotal; I don't actually know which one is more common. I just happen to know more cooks than people with fireplaces.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=775615#post775615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Honestly, the only reason why people don't use Wrought Iron is that it's an objectively worse material compared to iron that has been tempered into &amp;quot;steel.&amp;quot; Again, this is another reason why firearms would be better than weaponry against the True Fae, it's cheap and effective to make aggravated damage bullets, but considerably more difficult to do so with actual functional swords. I believe that is an issue to be addressed;. Now you might say it's impossible to get Wrought Iron, and certainly it's much less common now but certain things still use them. <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;http://www.woodlanddirect.com/Pilgrim-30-Vintage-Iron-Single-Fireplace-Tools-Poker?gdftrk=gdfV23673_a_7c1677_a_7c8224_a_7c1142054&amp;gclid=Cj0KEQiAm-CyBRDx65nBhcmVtbIBEiQA7zm8ldUbypfCnjxtA22o6qgEfYPtzwxwQwsJcZXej2kAjV4aApNy8P8HAQ&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">Here's</a> something I found in five minutes. Though of course this is real-world stuff I am talking about. If the Gentry were a real threat I'd expect to see many more &amp;quot;Antique Wrought Iron Swordsmiths&amp;quot; putting out advertisements with tongue-and-cheek references to warding off faeries.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't say it was impossible, just that commercial production had pretty much died. No factories produce large quantities of wrought iron anymore. It is still produced by some specialty sellers, but most of what you will find is mild steel. A lot of the time, sellers will advertise something as wrought iron when it just has the look of wrought iron. That item specifically says &quot;forged from wrought iron&quot;, so it's probably legit. Unless the seller is unethical and engaging in false advertising. But if you just pick up a poker at somebodies house, it's fairly likely that it's mild steel with a faux finish. And a fence post is even less likely to be legit if it was built in the last half century.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T21:24:06-08:00","id":775785,"title":"","content":"Since wrought iron is commonly 2 percent slag, it'd very hard (if not impossible) to make buckshot out of it. All of that stony shit is going to wreck the barrel of even a shotgun. That's not even taking the amount of wear all that metal is going to do. You might have to replace your shotgun every couple dozen shots. There's a very good reason why very soft metals like lead are used to make bullets and shot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T21:36:48-08:00","id":775790,"title":"","content":"So, let me get straight here - <b>Rules as are now in 1ED are that Fae Bane as Wrought <i>and</i> not Smelted Iron?</b> Like late Stone Age technology? Because <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bronze_Age\" target=\"_blank\">smelting was possible in the Bronze Age</a> ( <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chalcolithic\" target=\"_blank\">Copper Age even</a> ).<br /> <br /> If yes - I understand rarity as Bane, but even in Middle Ages this kind of Iron would be not possible to find. I think that <b>Chanegling</b> rules should emulate something like that in Middle Ages could be last time possible mass Fae Hunts - or rather organized Hunts. Later than that is the industry coming in to process ( in renaissance ), and limiting to earlier technology era would make Iron Bane unattainable in modern world - like Hand Wrought and not Smelted Iron. Also, Middle Ages are the last period we have legends of Fae kind coming from on large, so it would be good boundary for the most &quot;folk understanding&quot; the Gentries rules.<br /> <br /> Also, comparing to Werewolf's Silver and Vampires &amp; Prometheans Fire it's Hand Wrought and not Smelted Iron is insanely rare...<br /> <br /> As to <i>smelted Iron Bullets working as Bane</i> - I'm okay with that. You still <i>need</i> someone to blacksmith them - all the time - as people miss them. Great idea for Summer Courtier to become blacksmith for the Freehold and make all the time weapon and bullets to fight Fae!<br /> <br /> Until you cannot just go to the shop and ask for 4 kilograms of True Fae Bane in shape of bullets, I'm all for the basic smelting usage of Iron as &quot;Cold&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-28-2015, 12:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T21:49:53-08:00","id":775798,"title":"","content":"Huh. Just learned something new. Wrought iron is an alloy. ~98% iron and 2% slag (stones and rocks). Hand wrought iron means blacksmith forged wrought iron. So if it's the craftsmanship that is the main factor then I'd say any kind of artisan forged iron (whether its steel or wrought iron) should be effective. If, on the other hand, it's the slag in the alloy that makes the difference, then it shouldn't matter if it's hand forged or mass produced.<br /> <br /> Also, let me reiterate how quickly iron bullets are going to wreck your gun's barrel. Definitely not a good idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T22:14:18-08:00","id":775807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=775785#post775785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since wrought iron is commonly 2 percent slag, it'd very hard (if not impossible) to make buckshot out of it. All of that stony shit is going to wreck the barrel of even a shotgun. That's not even taking the amount of wear all that metal is going to do. You might have to replace your shotgun every couple dozen shots. There's a very good reason why very soft metals like lead are used to make bullets and shot.</div> </div> </div> </div>You probably wouldn't use wrought iron for bullets and shot. Cast iron would be the easiest, I'd think. You could probably also modify the mold used to make pig iron so that it produced bullets or shot instead of &quot;piglets.&quot; You might be able to use pelletized iron ore, but it may not be pure enough due to the additives needed to bind the pellets together. And yes, it would be harder on your barrel, but having to repair or replace your shotgun after fighting the Gentry is a small price to pay for such a potent weapon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T22:17:13-08:00","id":775808,"title":"","content":"Guess spending those experiences on a gunsmith specialty for Crafts is going to pay off. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T22:35:06-08:00","id":775812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=775808#post775808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guess spending those experiences on a gunsmith specialty for Crafts is going to pay off. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Or a gunsmith ally. Or enough dots of resources to buy a lot of shotguns. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T23:23:46-08:00","id":775821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=775798#post775798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, let me reiterate how quickly iron bullets are going to wreck your gun's barrel. Definitely not a good idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dramatic Failures on confrontation with True Fae are a b@#ch. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> When we are on topic - <b>How would you simulate that guns can randomly stop to work when using Iron Bullets?</b><br /> <br /> I imagine scene when, let's say, 10 Summer Courtiers are facing Gentry. <b>How to point when each of them has damages his weapon?<br /> <br /> Are there some rules for jamming the earlier pistols in <i>Dark Eras</i> we could use?</b><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T01:10:28-08:00","id":775855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/773619-better-defined-cold-iron?p=775821#post775821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dramatic Failures on confrontation with True Fae are a b@#ch. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> When we are on topic - <b>How would you simulate that guns can randomly stop to work when using Iron Bullets?</b><br /> <br /> I imagine scene when, let's say, 10 Summer Courtiers are facing Gentry. <b>How to point when each of them has damages his weapon?<br /> <br /> Are there some rules for jamming the earlier pistols in <i>Dark Eras</i> we could use?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I think dramatic failures cover it well enough. Modern barrels are strong enough that chances are pretty good the gun would make it through at least one firefight, if not several. Perhaps if the guns aren't repaired or replaced you could start applying negative modifiers in successive combats or after x rounds are fired. It only really matters if you're running a game where iron firefights are a regular thing, which strikes me as unlikely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T20:02:49-08:00","id":776387,"title":"","content":"Wrought iron, like silver, shouldn't be that hard to find (it might even be your fire place poker), it just requires you to find it. That means that unless they are knowledgeable and\u200b hunting Fae your average street punk is going to be carrying steel weapons. The first thing a changeling should be taught upon entering a free hold is how to get his hands on a Fae bane weapon. The goal wasn't to make the Fae unkillable but to make most ignorant mortals vulnerable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T08:52:24-08:00","id":776610,"title":"","content":"Well, steel isn't going to cut it-there's still some rules as to what counts as screwing over the fae and not. It's just much more precise and given more room than before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T01:44:36-08:00","id":777626,"title":"","content":"Talking about guns and cold iron bullets, do guns actually work (well) in the Hedge, let alone Arcadia? Because the Gentry and their hobgoblin cousins are not exactly going to be common in the normal world. When facing other changelings you might as well use a normal gun, just as effective and a lot easier to buy <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Like I said earlier, when it comes to weapons the issue of cold iron has never come up in my games. Now, getting items to deal with fey magic seems to be much more likely to come up in a game. Than again, perhaps my players are not quick to grab their weapons...<br /> <br /> P.S. If you really are looking for a cold iron weapon, why bother with a sword? Spears and bows are easier to get and use. Although, I do like the idea of iron powder shots that function a bit like the salt shots from Supernatural <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T14:36:19-08:00","id":777918,"title":"","content":"I can't recall if that's one of those things the core talks about.<br /> <br /> I imagine we'll find some space to talk about it in The Hedge. It's one of those things I've always wondered how to set mechanically. Of course, it might get dropped too. Raygun Gothic is fae too, after all.<br /> <br /> On the iron weapons thing, I've always found I preferred knives and spear heads. Cold iron is not hard to get, but not necessarily super easy to get or even simply easy to work. Keeping the effort minimal leads to a lot of small items(on the metal front) that can be used again and again. Knives fit that bill, and spearheads work well for when you need some extra oomph.<br /> <br /> Fae in general prefer small, sneaky items to use, particularly if they have anything to do in Ironside(mortal world). It's hard to get away with swords and axes when you're hanging around La Defense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 12-01-2015, 05:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T21:51:13-08:00","id":781552,"title":"","content":"I've yet to play a session of WoD / C:tL, so take it with a grain of salt, but I've done a bit of reading and I've got my opinions:<br /> <br /> It's &quot;cold iron&quot; if the Storyteller says it is. The inconsistency in the RAW gives them wiggle room since the definition itself is incomplete, unknown, and/or subject to change over generations. Common steel isn't going to cut it (...pun not intended) for whatever reasons made steel and the forging processes conceptually different in human/Changeling/Whatever consciousness. Breaking the fourth wall a bit, the idea is that a person has to go through some additional trouble and/or expense to get a viable cold iron weapon. I tell my Storyteller that I want a cold iron weapon, ask NPC scholars for their opinions, and roll my Occult skill checks. I go on a quest to retrieve a cold iron antique, hand work a ferrous meteorite into a knife shape, or embark on a zany chain-of-deals quest to get a &quot;proven&quot; cold iron weapon from a rather attached owner who'll trade it for a rare baseball card that just happens to be on sale at the Goblin Market for the price of a colorless red dream. (Hmm... Can I sleep furiously to get one?)<br /> <br /> On &quot;supernatural&quot;: I simply think it's wrong-headed to acknowledge the category as meaningful beyond being a label for stuff we don't understand (yet?). There are rules that define how the world works, and we will never know all of them. To me, &quot;supernatural&quot; is a junk drawer category we put stuff into to give ourselves the illusion of understanding. As if everything we label as such had some proven common feature, aside from that poor understanding. We understand pretty well how the universe works in the absence of the Wyrd, Wyld, Wyrm, and whatevyr the wryters dream up. The WoD is a place that adds an additional variety of strange forces and variables that make a mess of our understanding of how the world works IRL. By design, these exotic forces and entities produce plot devices for a horror/mystery story. The data are noisy and sparse, but those people reading the Occult section are good at generating working hypotheses. If they're wrong, you'll just have to go to your backup plan. Or accept your doom.<br /> <br /> Horror is about uncertainty and the fear the unknown brings. We don't know what exactly makes something &quot;cold iron&quot; or why it works against the Gentry. We just have some lore that's risen out of a dubious set of seemingly conflicting data. If you can guarantee that my cold iron knife will work against my Keeper because the rules in the book absolutely define &quot;cold iron&quot;, you remove a piece of that uncertainty. &quot;Did I mess something up when making it? Is there some technicality we don't know about that I missed?&quot; Clear knowledge is empowering. Horror is about lacking power, and mystery is about lacking knowledge.<br /> <br /> This isn't a chess tournament where rules have to be objective, fair, and aboveboard. Players don't &quot;win&quot; in the WoD by understanding how to work a concrete board where the rules are the same from one game to the next, or even determined ahead of time. This is a game where we have to trust a human Storyteller (you are human, right? ...Right?) to direct an engaging experience and not abuse that trust for the lulz of a Killer GM or to play favorites among the players. If your character wants to know how stuff bumps in the night or better ways of bumping back, well, he'll have to perform experiments just like we do in real life, get results from the Storyteller's description of the outcomes, and maybe, just maybe, he'll learn a little bit more and live to share that kernel of knowledge with future generations.<br /> <br /> Repeat to yourself, 'it's just a show. I really should relax.' For Mystery Science Theater 3000!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T22:35:18-08:00