ng the players. If your character wants to know how stuff bumps in the night or better ways of bumping back, well, he'll have to perform experiments just like we do in real life, get results from the Storyteller's description of the outcomes, and maybe, just maybe, he'll learn a little bit more and live to share that kernel of knowledge with future generations.<br /> <br /> Repeat to yourself, 'it's just a show. I really should relax.' For Mystery Science Theater 3000!</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree (if somewhat jealous I couldn't be quite so articulate...).<br /> <br /> Also, the emphasised text is hilarious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T10:47:27-08:00","id":781752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They're beings of stories from long ago when we knew little about the world. One of the reasons why Iron is supposed to be effective against them is because smelted, highly pure iron is unnatural and thus the antithesis of the Fae.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with the first sentence of this quote completely. I would say your &quot;antithesis to nature&quot; theory makes steel, plastic, concrete, drywall, lead paint, asbestos, and almost modern surface found in any western civilization would burn the True Fae, which wouldn't make a good story, which is more reliable descriptor of True Fae and Fairy Tales, than 'Embodies Nature' which your theory implicitly presumes. The Pied Piper, Cinderella's Fairy Godmother, The Frog Prince, and many other fairy tale characters who'd serve well in a Chronicle as a True Fae were not an agent or embodiment of nature.<br /> <br /> While it is true many fairies represented natural phenomenon or places, such as pixies, sprites, nymphs, kelpies, drowning hags, and some incarnations of elves, others do not fit that category like household brownies/hobs, leprechauns, red caps and many other creatures. The noteworthy stories told about these creatures are their most common denominator.<br /> <br /> Also looking at the history of iron based superstitions, it had power over witches, ghosts, foul spirits, the fair folk, and many malevolent supernatural beings and forces. One point was the insertion of an iron nail into the head of a corpse to prevent it from rising as a vampire.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also my dear friend, everything is chemistry.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here I must disagree with you. For how the True Fae and Arcadia is described, portrayed, and explained, it seem literally true that for them the universe isn't made of atoms, but of stories. I mean &quot;literally&quot; in the sense of exactly as written without figure of speech. For a True Fae or in Arcadia it seems that the notion of 'Atoms' or even basic physics are not only meaningless but also completely inaccurate to cover any of the phenomenon internal to the True Fae or Arcadia. I would not be surprised in the slightest if an electron microscope, spectrometer, or even litmus paper from a a grade school chemistry set failed to get readings, got nonsensical readings (like an electron microscope producing a picture of a the True Fae face when used on a drop of water in its realm), or non-reproducible and thus non-scientific results.<br /> <br /> True Fae and Arcadia give license to hang up a sign that reads &quot;science need not apply&quot;.<br /> <br /> Now to my theory why iron that has not been shaped by magic or machine is because iron has a magical property, perhaps because it has consistently and cross culturally played role as enemy of evil forces since truly ancient times, which is blotted out by other &quot;magic&quot; (to included more advanced technologies). I borrow the idea that technology is a form of hedge magic practicable by anyone with the knowledge from Mage the Ascension, which is very appropriate because of all the current supernatural types True Fae best embody non-objective reality based on concepts and/or belief.<br /> <br /> How would I define Wrought Iron in my chronicle? I would say I'd make a distinction between <a href=\"http://www.realwroughtiron.com/about_wrought_iron-217.html\" target=\"_blank\">Wrought Iron</a> and <a href=\"http://www.steelforge.com/literature/ferrousnon-ferrous-materials-textbook/ferrous-metals/carbon-steel/\" target=\"_blank\">Wrought Steel</a>. The distinction would be slag, non alloyed silicon impurities which are mechanically present and increase the brittleness and jaggedness of the metal when it is snapped. The difference between cast and wrought would also be important, the metal being worked by a blacksmith by hand. I would rule these work in the same way condition catches for fae contracts, or listening to Radio Free Fae. I would keep the it can't be worked by magic or cut by machine because those sound like clauses and loopholes that fit the flavor of how True Fae deal with reality. Does that mean my tiny diamond edged drill bit and power drill that I use to punch a small inconspicuous hole in the tang of your dagger and replace the handle wrapping would stop your &quot;wrought iron dagger&quot; from working when you needed it most? Absolutely! Welcome to the paranoia of the Lost.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> On the topic of &quot;iron bullets&quot; any problems would be caused by guns that use rifling, like all modern pistols and obviously rifles. You know what type of gun doesn't use rifling? Shotguns, even semi-automatic or fully-automatic shotguns.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Automatic_shotgun#/media/File:USAS12shotgun4104.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Picture of Fully Automatic Shotgun</a><br /> <br /> Just saying...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 12-07-2015, 03:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}